WEBVTT

0
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:11.800
Paayum Puli - Team MJY - WWW.MovieJockey.Com

1
00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:58.084
- The Thakur...?
-Welcome, sir. This way...

2
00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:47.280
I knew it the moment I received
your letter, Thakur...


3
00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.684
...that you wished to meet me.

4
00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.347
I took the first available train.

5
00:04:51.524 --> 00:04:54.982
I'm putting you to
some trouble, jailer.

6
00:04:55.061 --> 00:04:57.859
Not at all, sir. Just name it...
whatever it be.

7
00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:02.061
- I need two men.
- Two?

8
00:05:18.785 --> 00:05:20.252
Do you recognize them?

9
00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:24.646
There's hardly a prison where
they have not been held, Thakur.

10
00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:28.860
This is Veeru.
...and this is Jai.

11
00:05:29.962 --> 00:05:33.989
They're crooks, both of them.
Thieves of the first order.


12
00:05:34.801 --> 00:05:36.234
I know.

13
00:05:38.571 --> 00:05:43.770
They're just what I need
for the assignment at hand.

14
00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:47.946
I can't say what assignment
you have in mind, Thakur.

15
00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:51.772
But I can surely tell you that
they're good for nothing.

16
00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.418
That's not true, jailer.

17
00:05:55.321 --> 00:06:00.588
For all their vices, they
have some virtues, too.

18
00:06:01.661 --> 00:06:04.357
A fake coin is a fake, sir.
Whichever way you look at it.

19
00:06:05.565 --> 00:06:08.557
That is perhaps the difference
between man and coin.

20
00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.636
I clearly remember what
happened two years ago.

21
00:06:16.376 --> 00:06:19.812
I had arrested both of them
in district Jamalpur.

22
00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:24.413
We had to reach the police station
at village Tamli by dusk.

23
00:06:25.818 --> 00:06:27.649
Since no other arrangements
could be made...

24
00:06:29.088 --> 00:06:31.386
...we took a goods-train.


25
00:06:32.492 --> 00:06:35.393
I had two constables with me.
And there were these crooks...

26
00:06:40.032 --> 00:06:40.293
...Jaidev and Veeru;
chained and handcuffed.

27
00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:45.165
Could you have been at the Daulatpur
police station earlier, sir?

28
00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:48.771
Yes, I was. Why did you ask?


29
00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:50.736
I remember now!

30
00:06:51.411 --> 00:06:54.608
I've been wondering where I've seen
you, ever since you've caught us.


31
00:06:55.248 --> 00:06:57.239
Remember Lalji's shop? The
provision store which we robbed?

32
00:06:58.084 --> 00:07:01.918
- Do you remember?
- The provisioy store? no...

33
00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:04.222
Don't you? Jai...

34
00:07:05.057 --> 00:07:08.788
Remember, we were held at
the Daulatpur police station?

35
00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:10.987
- Daulatpur?
- Yes, don't you remember?

36
00:07:11.898 --> 00:07:16.096
- When was that?
- We had robbed the grocer...

37
00:07:16.569 --> 00:07:20.505
He was the officer then...
Don't you recognize him?

38
00:07:21.340 --> 00:07:24.503
All police officers
look the same to me.

39
00:07:26.846 --> 00:07:30.338
I can't help it, you know...
He's always talking nonsense.

40
00:07:31.751 --> 00:07:35.517
Since when have the two of you
been in this racket?

41
00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:40.792
You could say, we stood our own
two feet, the moment we could!

42
00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:42.652
But why must you do all this?

43
00:07:43.262 --> 00:07:46.231
The reason what you're a cop for...
we into it for the money.


44
00:07:47.099 --> 00:07:51.126
Not true. I'm not a police officer
just for the money.

45
00:07:52.104 --> 00:07:54.834
I have enough of family land
to keep us going.

46
00:07:56.209 --> 00:08:00.111
But perhaps I'm fond of the
dangers involved in the game.

47
00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.838
We face dangers everyday, too.

48
00:08:03.115 --> 00:08:08.280
There's a difference. I take on
dangers to protect the law.

49
00:08:09.055 --> 00:08:11.819
And you do it to
break the law.

50
00:08:12.091 --> 00:08:16.050
You need to be a brave man,
in both the cases.

51
00:08:16.128 --> 00:08:17.857
Oh sure! You do need courage.

52
00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:20.488
I see.

53
00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.734
You guys think you're
very brave, don't you?

54
00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:27.032
You will see when
the need arises, Inspector.

55
00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:29.507
We'd at least take on
15 or 20 guys.

56
00:08:30.243 --> 00:08:32.370
I haven't exaggerated it,
have I?

57
00:08:32.712 --> 00:08:35.943
- Now that you've already said it...
- We deal with it!

58
00:08:47.293 --> 00:08:48.453
Bandits!

59
00:09:04.277 --> 00:09:06.370
Well, Inspector?
Want to try out our guts?

60
00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:15.477
There's still time, Inspector.
Give it a thought!

61
00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:28.128
Don't you try to escape.

62
00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:09.832
Stop the engine, driver!

63
00:10:16.749 --> 00:10:20.116
Let's move ahead!
As fast as you can!

64
00:10:45.411 --> 00:10:46.844
Charge ahead!

65
00:13:33.045 --> 00:13:34.876
Give me a swig! Quick!

66
00:15:45.177 --> 00:15:47.145
-Are you okay?
- I'm all right...

67
00:16:17.343 --> 00:16:19.208
He dares mess with Veeru!

68
00:16:26.418 --> 00:16:28.409
They've fled, the swines!

69
00:16:28.620 --> 00:16:30.679
Let's go... Come on!

70
00:16:32.624 --> 00:16:37.652
I had warned you
not to escape...

71
00:16:46.638 --> 00:16:47.605
What do you think?

72
00:16:47.706 --> 00:16:49.071
We can run away.

73
00:16:50.743 --> 00:16:52.574
Leaving him in this state?

74
00:16:52.978 --> 00:16:54.673
He's going no die, if we
Leave him in this condition.

75
00:16:56.715 --> 00:16:58.148
Suppose we take him
to the hospital...

76
00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:01.117
...we get sent away
for four or six months.

77
00:17:01.787 --> 00:17:04.551
- So what do you suggest?
-What do you think?

78
00:17:06.025 --> 00:17:07.720
Get it out.

79
00:17:11.330 --> 00:17:15.323
If it's Heads, we go to the hospital;
If it's Tails, we escape.

80
00:17:25.911 --> 00:17:30.211
They are criminals, no doubt.
But they're terribly brave.

81
00:17:31.050 --> 00:17:34.850
They are dangerous, because
they know how to fight back.

82
00:17:35.888 --> 00:17:39.119
They're bad... but they're human.

83
00:17:40.459 --> 00:17:45.556
Could you find these
guys for me, jailer?

84
00:17:47.199 --> 00:17:50.965
We'll easily find them, if they
are presenly in some prison.

85
00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:55.228
But if they're free, it's
difficuln to find such people.

86
00:24:27.199 --> 00:24:29.759
Soorma Bhopali! You're pulling
oun more of the firewood.

87
00:24:29.835 --> 00:24:32.929
Naturally. You don't expect me
to put some more, do you?

88
00:24:33.004 --> 00:24:36.997
The scale says it's enough...
and you insist on more.

89
00:24:37.075 --> 00:24:39.942
just take the wood and get going.
Give me the money...

90
00:24:41.012 --> 00:24:41.944
Here's a 2-Rupee bill.

91
00:24:42.047 --> 00:24:45.881
I can see that, but is it genuine?
okay, it is.

92
00:24:45.951 --> 00:24:49.751
So then, good-bye.

93
00:24:50.288 --> 00:24:54.952
-Won't you return my moyey?
- Money? What money do you want?

94
00:24:55.026 --> 00:24:57.790
- That's a nwo-Rupee bill!
- The wood is worth 2 Rupees too!

95
00:24:57.863 --> 00:24:59.854
just this much of wood
for two Rupees ?!

96
00:24:59.931 --> 00:25:03.867
Were you out to buy the whole forest
for two bucks then?

97
00:25:03.935 --> 00:25:07.871
Now look; l've had enough!
Just get going.

98
00:25:07.939 --> 00:25:12.137
I'm not Soorma Bhopali for nothing!
okay?

99
00:25:12.244 --> 00:25:16.271
Get lost...
I wonder where they come from!

100
00:25:16.381 --> 00:25:19.839
He says the wood is too little!
Wants the forest then, does he?!

101
00:25:19.951 --> 00:25:22.920
They always come early every
morning to spoil my day!

102
00:25:22.988 --> 00:25:28.654
There, Chand! You're at your
cursed poetry again!

103
00:25:28.727 --> 00:25:31.594
Go and check if they're unloaded
the stuff from the truck yet!

104
00:25:32.664 --> 00:25:35.360
Well! Well! Are you guys
watching a drama here?

105
00:25:35.867 --> 00:25:38.301
This is no travellers' bungalow...
who are you guys?

106
00:25:42.607 --> 00:25:46.043
God Almighty! lt's you!

107
00:25:46.244 --> 00:25:48.041
How are you, Soorma Bhopali?

108
00:25:48.146 --> 00:25:51.240
I'm fine, thank you!

109
00:25:51.816 --> 00:25:54.046
But what are you guys up to?!

110
00:25:55.287 --> 00:25:56.447
Come here!

111
00:25:56.521 --> 00:26:01.652
The police have declared a reward
of 2000 Rupees for your arrest.

112
00:26:01.726 --> 00:26:06.925
If someone watches us together,
I'll land in trouble, too!

113
00:26:06.998 --> 00:26:08.693
So please get going!

114
00:26:08.800 --> 00:26:11.860
Know what, Soorma Bhopali?
We want to go to prison.

115
00:26:11.937 --> 00:26:14.633
I hope God fulfills your wish!

116
00:26:14.706 --> 00:26:18.767
Had this been Bhopal, I'd have had
you locked up in just two minutes!

117
00:26:18.877 --> 00:26:21.675
I'm not Soorma Bhopali for
nothing, you know!

118
00:26:21.746 --> 00:26:23.873
But why would anyone
need me here?

119
00:26:23.982 --> 00:26:26.951
A warrant's out in
your name in any case!

120
00:26:27.152 --> 00:26:31.020
But we want you to
have us arrested.

121
00:26:31.423 --> 00:26:33.186
What are you talking about?!

122
00:26:33.258 --> 00:26:37.285
There's a reward of 2000 Rupees
which you will get.

123
00:26:37.362 --> 00:26:43.597
Give us half the money, when
we're released from prison.

124
00:26:44.269 --> 00:26:46.601
- Do you get it?
-What are you saying!

125
00:26:46.871 --> 00:26:52.935
Have some betel-leaf;
Go on... it's great!

126
00:27:01.953 --> 00:27:03.750
Since when have they started
having a parade here?

127
00:27:03.822 --> 00:27:07.656
You've just arrived, sonny boy.
You'll get to know soon.

128
00:27:07.726 --> 00:27:10.126
This new jailer is a nasty one!

129
00:27:10.428 --> 00:27:13.659
-A nasty jailer, he says.
- There he is.

130
00:27:32.751 --> 00:27:34.241
Attention, l say!

131
00:27:38.990 --> 00:27:41.618
But they're already
an attention, sir.

132
00:27:45.096 --> 00:27:47.530
I know that.

133
00:27:48.066 --> 00:27:49.590
Prisoners!
This is a warning for you!

134
00:27:50.602 --> 00:27:56.165
Everythiyg that went unchecked
before my arrival here...

135
00:27:56.241 --> 00:27:59.142
...will no longer be tolerated!

136
00:28:03.014 --> 00:28:06.814
I've been a jailer since
the British days!

137
00:28:07.485 --> 00:28:09.612
I don't belong to the breed
of jailers...

138
00:28:09.688 --> 00:28:13.351
...who waste time, trying to
reform the prisoners!

139
00:28:14.693 --> 00:28:19.528
l know it for a fact!
You guys can't be reformed!

140
00:28:19.597 --> 00:28:23.556
How can you ever change,
when I have not changed?

141
00:28:29.107 --> 00:28:33.134
I know, my words don't
go down well with you.

142
00:28:33.978 --> 00:28:39.177
Which is why I am transferred
from every place I work in.

143
00:28:40.251 --> 00:28:46.679
But despite all my transfers...
I have not changed!

144
00:28:48.860 --> 00:28:50.452
So you'd better remember!

145
00:28:50.528 --> 00:28:55.431
Don't think I am not informed
of all that you guys are up to!

146
00:28:56.101 --> 00:29:02.006
I have spies everywhere
in the prison.

147
00:29:02.273 --> 00:29:05.299
I get a report of every moment.

148
00:29:06.277 --> 00:29:09.269
Not even a bird could
flap its wings here...

149
00:29:09.380 --> 00:29:11.712
...without my consent!

150
00:29:12.083 --> 00:29:14.608
-What the hell was that?!
-A bird... a pigeon, sir!

151
00:29:14.686 --> 00:29:17.382
What's that in my eyes...
never mind!

152
00:29:18.189 --> 00:29:22.057
This will do for today!
You may leave now.

153
00:29:26.765 --> 00:29:27.925
Let's go!

154
00:29:30.935 --> 00:29:32.664
Strange guy!

155
00:29:33.438 --> 00:29:35.770
Who could be the jailer's spy?

156
00:29:36.407 --> 00:29:40.002
I know that.
It's the barber, Hariram.

157
00:29:40.111 --> 00:29:43.740
He's very thick with the jailer.
The swine!

158
00:29:44.048 --> 00:29:45.515
Hariram, the barber?

159
00:29:52.891 --> 00:29:55.587
Go ahead and shave
my moustache, Hariram.

160
00:29:57.162 --> 00:30:00.029
It has all been arranged!

161
00:30:00.098 --> 00:30:02.794
We get cracking tomorrow.

162
00:30:02.867 --> 00:30:06.894
How many days will it take
to make the tunnel?

163
00:30:07.772 --> 00:30:09.262
You've cut my face!

164
00:30:09.340 --> 00:30:14.243
The tunnel? lt should be
ready iy about a week.

165
00:30:15.180 --> 00:30:18.172
Where are we going to
dig the tunnel from?

166
00:30:18.416 --> 00:30:21.715
It's from Barrack No. 9.

167
00:30:21.786 --> 00:30:24.949
I hope the jailer
doesn,t get to know!

168
00:30:25.023 --> 00:30:28.982
No one will hear of it!

169
00:30:32.297 --> 00:30:33.787
Let's go!

170
00:30:35.900 --> 00:30:38.198
There. l'm through.

171
00:30:46.511 --> 00:30:49.344
Yes, Hariram?
What news do you bring?

172
00:30:49.414 --> 00:30:53.510
Be careful, sir. They're digging
a tunnel in the jail.

173
00:30:53.952 --> 00:30:57.649
oh, well! tunnel in my jail...

174
00:30:59.190 --> 00:31:01.283
What was that? A tunnel
in my jail ?!

175
00:31:01.359 --> 00:31:03.919
Yes, sir. The prisoners are
making a tunnel in the jail.

176
00:31:04.462 --> 00:31:07.260
I've been a jailer since
the days of the British!

177
00:31:07.966 --> 00:31:12.130
A tunnel in my jail, eh?

178
00:31:38.863 --> 00:31:42.458
So this is where the
tunnel is being dug!

179
00:31:43.034 --> 00:31:44.661
This is wonderful!

180
00:31:45.270 --> 00:31:48.398
But you guys seem to have
forgotten that my spies...

181
00:31:48.473 --> 00:31:53.274
...are spread out in
every part of the prison.

182
00:31:54.779 --> 00:31:56.076
And what is this?

183
00:32:01.419 --> 00:32:05.651
So this is the tool with which
you will dig the tunnel!

184
00:32:09.794 --> 00:32:14.197
I'm a jailer... from
the British days!

185
00:32:20.905 --> 00:32:22.372
Here he comes!

186
00:32:25.043 --> 00:32:28.012
- ls in all arranged then?
-Yes.

187
00:32:28.112 --> 00:32:31.548
We won't miss out this time!

188
00:32:31.883 --> 00:32:34.249
A pistol has arrived
in the prison!

189
00:32:34.319 --> 00:32:37.345
Has the pistol arrived?!

190
00:32:38.890 --> 00:32:47.093
In just a couple of days,
the jailer and his spies...

191
00:32:53.071 --> 00:32:55.505
A pistol in my prison, eh?

192
00:32:55.707 --> 00:32:59.040
A pistol in my prison,
did you say?!

193
00:32:59.143 --> 00:33:01.008
-A revolt?!
- Than's right.

194
00:33:01.079 --> 00:33:02.444
- Streams of blood?!
- Exactly.

195
00:33:02.513 --> 00:33:04.947
Guards!

196
00:33:12.123 --> 00:33:13.147
Halt!

197
00:33:14.525 --> 00:33:16.959
Search every nook and corner
of the jail!

198
00:33:17.628 --> 00:33:20.324
Half of you go in that direction.

199
00:33:21.432 --> 00:33:23.525
Half of you go there.

200
00:33:26.437 --> 00:33:30.737
The rest of you guys...
come with me!

201
00:34:40.211 --> 00:34:42.270
Here's the pistol!

202
00:34:43.247 --> 00:34:46.705
Move an inch, and...

203
00:34:48.453 --> 00:34:49.784
Guards!

204
00:34:49.854 --> 00:34:51.412
They've left.

205
00:34:53.558 --> 00:34:56.755
- Let's go to your office.
- How can I?

206
00:34:57.261 --> 00:34:58.819
You have asked me not to move!

207
00:34:58.896 --> 00:35:01.660
The firsn order sstands cancelled.
Let's go.

208
00:35:12.844 --> 00:35:17.110
lt the jailer of the British days
so scared?

209
00:35:19.016 --> 00:35:20.449
No!

210
00:35:21.886 --> 00:35:25.083
Come and see us off
at the gate first!

211
00:35:42.707 --> 00:35:44.470
Have the gate opened.

212
00:35:52.416 --> 00:35:53.974
open the gate.

213
00:36:04.762 --> 00:36:06.195
Here's the key.

214
00:36:08.966 --> 00:36:11.127
And here's the ''pistol'' !

215
00:36:15.806 --> 00:36:18.172
The two of them must have
tried to run away, isn't it?

216
00:36:18.242 --> 00:36:21.541
Tried to run away?
That's an understatement!

217
00:36:21.646 --> 00:36:23.443
They put their lives
into it!

218
00:36:23.514 --> 00:36:26.312
Bun I wasn't about
to let them go!

219
00:36:26.384 --> 00:36:28.614
As I held one of them...

220
00:36:28.686 --> 00:36:31.086
...the other tried to escape.

221
00:36:31.155 --> 00:36:35.057
I dragged him back and asked,
''Where to, feller?''

222
00:36:35.126 --> 00:36:38.721
With two stinging slaps, I ordered
them to the police station!

223
00:36:38.796 --> 00:36:41.424
That was it! They were
begging at my feet!

224
00:36:41.866 --> 00:36:44.061
Did Veeru and jai really
beg an your feet?

225
00:36:44.135 --> 00:36:45.659
They're dangerous criminals!

226
00:36:45.736 --> 00:36:48.227
They're criminals, all right!

227
00:36:48.306 --> 00:36:53.073
But I'm not called Soorma
Bhopali for nothing!

228
00:36:53.511 --> 00:36:56.912
You can imagine!
They wept at my feet!

229
00:36:57.048 --> 00:37:00.347
And begged for forgiveness;
I'd have forgiven them, too!

230
00:37:00.418 --> 00:37:05.185
But I was furious than they had
dared to trespass my territory!

231
00:37:05.256 --> 00:37:07.884
-What happened next?
-What else?!

232
00:37:07.959 --> 00:37:09.756
You know I carry a stick!

233
00:37:09.827 --> 00:37:13.763
It was days since I had used it.
So I got down to brass-tracks...

234
00:37:13.831 --> 00:37:17.733
...and I really thrashed them!
I gave them a terrible beating!

235
00:37:17.802 --> 00:37:20.100
-What happened next?
-What would have happened?

236
00:37:20.171 --> 00:37:24.870
I held them by their collars
ayd said...

237
00:37:24.942 --> 00:37:27.911
-What did you say?
-What did I ?!

238
00:37:27.979 --> 00:37:30.573
What did I say?!
Yes, I remember...

239
00:37:30.681 --> 00:37:34.310
I said, ''Do let me know if there is
something more I can do for you''

240
00:37:34.385 --> 00:37:38.287
Well, guys... have you
nothing better to do?

241
00:37:38.356 --> 00:37:41.917
You plunk yourselves here and
compel me to concoct falsehoods!

242
00:37:41.993 --> 00:37:46.987
Go and attend to your work!
Go on... lazy bums!

243
00:37:48.065 --> 00:37:51.159
Well,... I was oyly kidding.

244
00:37:51.235 --> 00:37:55.433
But you guys have been released
pretty quickly, haven't you?

245
00:37:55.506 --> 00:38:01.274
My word! The stint at the prison
seems to have been good foryou!

246
00:38:01.379 --> 00:38:05.475
We are here to collect
our thousand Rupees.

247
00:38:05.583 --> 00:38:09.349
-A thousand rupees?
- That's right. A thousand bucks.

248
00:38:09.453 --> 00:38:11.580
I see!

249
00:38:11.656 --> 00:38:15.319
I got the money the very next day
of your arrest!

250
00:38:15.393 --> 00:38:20.922
Since that day, the money has been
lyiyg in an envelope in my pocket!

251
00:38:20.998 --> 00:38:23.899
Check it out...
it's a thousand bucks!

252
00:38:23.968 --> 00:38:27.199
Well, Soorma... see you again.

253
00:38:39.150 --> 00:38:40.947
It's these chaps I've
been lookiyg for.

254
00:38:41.018 --> 00:38:43.987
When does their prison term
come to an end?

255
00:38:44.055 --> 00:38:47.855
on the 18th of the next month.

256
00:38:53.597 --> 00:38:56.327
Could I have a beedi, guard?

257
00:39:12.616 --> 00:39:16.416
Well, Inspector? Who have you
brought to the prison today?

258
00:39:17.755 --> 00:39:21.282
I'm not an Inspector anymore.
I'm just Thakur Baldev Singh.

259
00:39:22.326 --> 00:39:27.457
Why? Have you gotten overyour
fondness of playiyg with dangers?

260
00:39:29.233 --> 00:39:32.760
If your bravery really makes
you so arrogant...

261
00:39:34.839 --> 00:39:36.807
...will you accept
an assignment from me?

262
00:39:37.541 --> 00:39:40.510
We accept assignments
oyly for money.

263
00:39:41.245 --> 00:39:42.337
How much do you want?

264
00:39:47.985 --> 00:39:49.316
What's the job?

265
00:39:49.754 --> 00:39:52.484
Why must you worry about that,
if you're really brave?

266
00:39:53.924 --> 00:39:56.791
Name the price.
And you will get it.

267
00:39:56.861 --> 00:40:00.126
Provided you do what
I want you to do.

268
00:40:02.066 --> 00:40:06.002
Gabbar Singh?!
The notorious bandit?!

269
00:40:06.070 --> 00:40:08.197
Yes. He's the one.

270
00:40:08.372 --> 00:40:11.398
The police are even said no have
placed a reward on his head.

271
00:40:11.475 --> 00:40:16.037
-50,000 Rupees... for capturing him
dead or alive.

272
00:40:16.814 --> 00:40:21.410
You've got to capture the
bandit for me... alive.

273
00:40:21.652 --> 00:40:24.746
You want us to get Gabbar Singh...
that too, alive ayd kicking!

274
00:40:25.356 --> 00:40:29.190
Gabbar Singh is no sheep-kid
we could run and catch, Thakur!

275
00:40:30.060 --> 00:40:32.392
I know it's a difficult task.

276
00:40:33.364 --> 00:40:36.527
But no one pays so much
for something easy.

277
00:40:37.201 --> 00:40:40.659
Let's suppose we risk our lives and
somehow manage to capture him.

278
00:40:41.305 --> 00:40:44.672
Do you want us to hand him over
to you for just 20,000 Rupees?

279
00:40:45.209 --> 00:40:46.904
So you can make a cool
50,000 Rupees, for nothing?

280
00:40:47.878 --> 00:40:50.676
The reward from the police
will go to you, too.

281
00:40:51.048 --> 00:40:53.676
I only want Gabbar.

282
00:40:54.418 --> 00:40:57.114
Is it ay old feud?

283
00:40:59.323 --> 00:41:02.486
That's none of your business.

284
00:41:05.763 --> 00:41:07.560
May I ask you another
question then?

285
00:41:08.232 --> 00:41:12.168
You know we're criminals, too.

286
00:41:12.236 --> 00:41:16.639
Why did you choose us
to track down the bandit?

287
00:41:16.707 --> 00:41:21.644
Only because iron
shall deal with iron.

288
00:41:27.251 --> 00:41:28.878
That's 5,000 Rupees.

289
00:41:29.286 --> 00:41:32.084
You will get 5,000 more upon
your arrival in Ramgarh.

290
00:41:32.590 --> 00:41:35.354
The rest afteryou have
accomplished the mission.

291
00:41:41.332 --> 00:41:43.926
What do you suggest?

292
00:41:53.310 --> 00:41:57.303
''Heads'' -we go.

293
00:42:17.668 --> 00:42:19.795
Well, gentlemen?
Where will you go?

294
00:42:19.870 --> 00:42:22.998
Belapur, Rampur, Ramgarh...
where do you want to go?

295
00:42:24.608 --> 00:42:28.442
Have you never seen
a horse-cart before?

296
00:42:28.512 --> 00:42:30.036
This is a village, sir.

297
00:42:30.147 --> 00:42:34.311
You can't find cars here in
which you can speed away.

298
00:42:34.385 --> 00:42:36.683
Basanti's "tonga" is all
you will find around here.

299
00:42:36.754 --> 00:42:39.848
Now look; I'm not in the habit
of talking unnecessarily.

300
00:42:39.924 --> 00:42:42.552
- Say so, if you wish to go...
-Well, we do wish...

301
00:42:42.626 --> 00:42:46.960
It's okay, if you don't wish to go!
You won't be my enemies!

302
00:42:47.031 --> 00:42:50.125
I thought you'd need a tonga
and happened to ask you.

303
00:42:50.200 --> 00:42:52.691
But you don't have to be
my passengers, you know.

304
00:42:52.770 --> 00:42:54.601
It's your own free will!

305
00:42:54.672 --> 00:42:57.937
This is Basanti's tonga, not
the field of the landlord...

306
00:42:58.008 --> 00:43:00.169
...which you will have to till,
even if you don't want to!

307
00:43:00.277 --> 00:43:03.940
- This is just like...
- Let's go! We wish to go!

308
00:43:04.048 --> 00:43:07.381
- Let's go!
- Sure. When have l refused?

309
00:43:07.451 --> 00:43:10.818
Now look; I'm not a chatter-box.

310
00:43:10.888 --> 00:43:13.288
So I'd better tell you in advance.

311
00:43:13.357 --> 00:43:16.554
A ride to Belapur costs 2 Rupees
and one to Rampur costs 1 .5 Rupee.

312
00:43:16.627 --> 00:43:19.687
Don't haggle, please!
What Basanti says is final!

313
00:43:19.763 --> 00:43:22.095
- okay, but we...
- I know what you will say!

314
00:43:22.166 --> 00:43:26.796
Just why I charge 2 Rupees for
Belapur and 1.50 for Ramgarh?

315
00:43:26.870 --> 00:43:30.067
You'd better ask which village
this tonga belongs to. Go on.

316
00:43:31.342 --> 00:43:34.311
- Well, where does it belong?
- It belongs to Ramgarh!

317
00:43:34.411 --> 00:43:36.504
I see! So it belongs
to Ramgarh! Now I know!

318
00:43:37.681 --> 00:43:39.615
Actually, there is this thing
worth considering.

319
00:43:39.683 --> 00:43:42.880
When I make a trip to Belapur,
I actually make two trips.

320
00:43:42.953 --> 00:43:45.114
To Belapur and back to Ramgarh.

321
00:43:45.189 --> 00:43:50.752
But should I go to Ramgarh,
it's like going home.

322
00:43:51.128 --> 00:43:55.121
Where would you like to go?

323
00:43:55.199 --> 00:43:57.861
Actually, we'd like
to go to Ramgarh, too.

324
00:43:57.935 --> 00:44:00.426
Sure! When have I refused?

325
00:44:00.504 --> 00:44:03.803
But you will have to tell me
whose house you're going to.

326
00:44:04.041 --> 00:44:06.305
So Basanti can take you
to that house.

327
00:44:06.410 --> 00:44:10.073
If I'm not told where
you've got to go...

328
00:44:10.180 --> 00:44:11.613
...how will I stop the tonga?

329
00:44:11.715 --> 00:44:14.684
How will the tonga stop
if I don't stop it?

330
00:44:14.785 --> 00:44:20.246
Who holds the reins?
I do!

331
00:44:20.324 --> 00:44:21.723
And if I......

332
00:44:21.792 --> 00:44:25.023
We've got to go to Thakur
Baldev Singh's place.

333
00:44:26.397 --> 00:44:28.627
Sure! Let's go!
When did I refuse?

334
00:44:28.699 --> 00:44:30.758
You could said as much!

335
00:44:30.834 --> 00:44:33.200
Let's go, Dhanno!

336
00:44:40.844 --> 00:44:45.110
So you see, I had already
lost my parents.

337
00:44:45.616 --> 00:44:49.916
And who had to fend for my aunt
and ply the tonga?

338
00:44:49.987 --> 00:44:51.113
Me, of course.

339
00:44:51.188 --> 00:44:56.717
People ask how a girl like me
can go around plying a tonga.

340
00:44:57.294 --> 00:44:59.762
I have an answer ready
for them.

341
00:45:00.264 --> 00:45:02.858
Dhanno is a mare; and she
can still draw the cart.

342
00:45:03.400 --> 00:45:06.233
So why not Basanti?
Am I right?

343
00:45:06.303 --> 00:45:10.763
So what's wrong? City girls drive
cars... no one says anything to them.

344
00:45:11.709 --> 00:45:15.475
You're a wise man, although
you're from the city.

345
00:45:15.579 --> 00:45:18.844
- What is your name?
- Veeru.

346
00:45:18.916 --> 00:45:21.714
You haven't yet asked me
my name, have you?

347
00:45:21.785 --> 00:45:23.912
What is your name, Basanti?

348
00:45:23.987 --> 00:45:26.956
Oh, shut up! You're always
talking nonsense!

349
00:45:27.024 --> 00:45:30.187
I wasn't talking to you, you know.

350
00:45:30.260 --> 00:45:33.957
But since you have asked me,
let me tell you...

351
00:45:34.031 --> 00:45:35.259
...my name is Basanti.

352
00:45:35.332 --> 00:45:37.926
Than's nhe firsn nime
I've heard the name.

353
00:45:38.202 --> 00:45:41.638
Basanti! What a lovely name!

354
00:45:42.106 --> 00:45:45.633
There's a story
behind my name, too.

355
00:45:45.709 --> 00:45:47.904
Really? Do tell me... !

356
00:45:48.011 --> 00:45:50.878
When I was a little girl...

357
00:45:50.948 --> 00:45:54.315
...a distant relative said...

358
00:46:11.168 --> 00:46:13.636
That's it, Dhanno! Halt!

359
00:46:13.704 --> 00:46:16.639
This is the Thakur's mansion.

360
00:46:16.807 --> 00:46:21.471
Strange! Talking to you guys,
I didn't even realize the distance.

361
00:46:21.578 --> 00:46:23.773
That's right.
We are very talkative.

362
00:46:23.881 --> 00:46:26.441
Here's the 1.50 Rupee
we had settled for.

363
00:46:26.550 --> 00:46:30.179
You're a nice man. I shouldn't be
accepting the money from you.

364
00:46:30.254 --> 00:46:33.382
But what will the horse eat,
if it befriends its food?

365
00:46:33.457 --> 00:46:37.757
- So I will accept the money.
- That's very kind of you.

366
00:46:40.030 --> 00:46:42.965
Let's go, Dhanno!

367
00:46:50.040 --> 00:46:53.203
Wow! She talks so well!

368
00:46:53.911 --> 00:46:56.436
She talks too much!

369
00:46:56.880 --> 00:47:00.111
Let's go. You don't have to
score with every girl you meet.

370
00:47:01.518 --> 00:47:02.883
Come on!

371
00:47:03.687 --> 00:47:05.052
Welcome.

372
00:47:09.226 --> 00:47:10.818
This way, please.

373
00:47:15.065 --> 00:47:16.498
Greetings, Thakur.

374
00:47:16.567 --> 00:47:18.865
You had no problems
getting here, I hope?

375
00:47:18.936 --> 00:47:21.234
Well, not much.

376
00:47:21.305 --> 00:47:23.136
Come in.

377
00:47:25.676 --> 00:47:28.804
Had you dropped a letter, I'd have
sent someone to receive you.

378
00:47:30.214 --> 00:47:32.614
Your stay has been arranged.

379
00:47:32.950 --> 00:47:35.942
Just let me know, if there
is anything you need.

380
00:47:45.662 --> 00:47:50.099
I had promised to pay you 5000
rupees on your arrival here.

381
00:47:53.670 --> 00:47:57.436
You remember your
assignment, don't you?

382
00:47:58.408 --> 00:48:00.672
I want Gabbar.

383
00:48:00.777 --> 00:48:03.109
- I want him alive.
- Of course, remember.

384
00:48:03.513 --> 00:48:07.677
You want Gabbar...
captured alive.

385
00:48:08.452 --> 00:48:09.851
You will have him.

386
00:48:10.687 --> 00:48:13.884
Go and take some rest.
You must be tired.

387
00:48:13.957 --> 00:48:16.152
We'll discuss the rest later.

388
00:48:16.226 --> 00:48:17.591
Follow me.

389
00:48:30.240 --> 00:48:34.006
Please go ahead.
I'll go and fetch the keys.

390
00:48:41.218 --> 00:48:45.018
That safe was
stuffed with riches!

391
00:48:45.923 --> 00:48:49.017
Folks in this village
seem to wear a lot of gold.

392
00:48:49.092 --> 00:48:51.253
So what do you say?

393
00:49:15.085 --> 00:49:19.852
Quite a big house...
and beautiful, too.

394
00:49:21.625 --> 00:49:24.526
- Who else stays in there?
- Your keys.

395
00:49:25.996 --> 00:49:27.327
That is your quarters.

396
00:49:27.397 --> 00:49:31.231
Do call me over, should
you need something.

397
00:49:34.004 --> 00:49:38.202
I can't quite figure this out.

398
00:49:38.275 --> 00:49:42.371
Why must we bother, Jai?
The Thakur has paid us 10,000.

399
00:49:42.479 --> 00:49:46.347
Let's clean out his safe tonight
and get away. What say?

400
00:49:48.218 --> 00:49:49.913
Very well.

401
00:49:50.187 --> 00:49:53.315
Let's sleep now, if we're going
to keep awake tonight.

402
00:51:30.187 --> 00:51:32.417
Thakur! These guys were...

403
00:51:32.489 --> 00:51:34.389
They're my men.

404
00:51:34.891 --> 00:51:37.018
TThen why did they attack us?

405
00:51:37.494 --> 00:51:43.899
I wanted to see if you still
possess the courage and strength.

406
00:51:43.967 --> 00:51:49.200
Or whether time has rendered
your might, impotent.

407
00:51:49.272 --> 00:51:52.708
So? What did you see?

408
00:51:52.909 --> 00:52:01.248
I see that I have made no mistake
in having you brought here.

409
00:52:04.754 --> 00:52:07.552
There is one mistake you
have made, Thakur!

410
00:52:08.191 --> 00:52:10.785
You have shown us the
cotnents of your safe.

411
00:53:33.677 --> 00:53:36.077
Here's the key to the safe.

412
00:53:38.415 --> 00:53:41.976
The safe has some ornaments
which are of no use to me.

413
00:53:43.286 --> 00:53:46.585
A widow will never need them again.

414
00:53:48.158 --> 00:53:51.821
It has some money, too.
You can take that away.

415
00:53:53.196 --> 00:53:57.462
I'm glad, it will at least break
the Thakur's false hopes.

416
00:53:58.368 --> 00:54:01.462
Hopes, that he has pinned on you.

417
00:54:13.250 --> 00:54:14.308
Excuse me.

418
00:54:37.274 --> 00:54:40.368
That which happened last night
will not happen again.

419
00:55:01.464 --> 00:55:02.431
Here... have some more!

420
00:55:02.632 --> 00:55:04.759
You've eaten enough
to be big and strong!

421
00:55:05.435 --> 00:55:08.836
But when we make to trip to Belapur,
you sure do put on airs!

422
00:55:09.639 --> 00:55:13.097
- Go ahead and eat...!
- Basanti...!

423
00:55:13.176 --> 00:55:15.872
I'm here, feeding
this donkey, auntie!

424
00:55:16.646 --> 00:55:19.137
Now watch her take off!

425
00:55:19.482 --> 00:55:23.612
Listen, lady!
You can roam around all day!

426
00:55:24.020 --> 00:55:26.250
But you wouldn't do
a simple chore for me!

427
00:55:28.658 --> 00:55:31.991
You're always losing
your temper with me, auntie.

428
00:55:32.062 --> 00:55:34.826
Won't you give me a chance?
What had you asked me to do?

429
00:55:34.964 --> 00:55:36.522
You asked me to go to
the physician, didn't you?

430
00:55:36.766 --> 00:55:39.633
I did go to him to
fetch your medicines.

431
00:55:39.703 --> 00:55:41.295
But he wasn't there.

432
00:55:41.671 --> 00:55:44.196
He's supposed to be ill...

433
00:55:44.274 --> 00:55:46.242
...and has gone to the neighboring
village for treatment.

434
00:55:46.309 --> 00:55:50.211
I didn't mention the doctor and
you gave me a whole lecture!

435
00:55:50.914 --> 00:55:52.779
What else did you ask me to do?

436
00:55:52.849 --> 00:55:55.010
Didn't I ask you to fetch some
raw mangoes for the pickle?

437
00:55:55.285 --> 00:55:57.344
But you will never remember!

438
00:55:58.221 --> 00:56:01.213
Oh sure, you did tell me!
I'll go and fetch them right away!

439
00:56:04.761 --> 00:56:07.559
Lmamsaheb! Do you want me
to reach you home?

440
00:56:07.630 --> 00:56:08.654
Who's that?

441
00:56:09.933 --> 00:56:12.731
Basanti! It's you today.

442
00:56:13.703 --> 00:56:16.069
I've spent years in this village.

443
00:56:16.639 --> 00:56:18.231
You weren't even born then.

444
00:56:18.742 --> 00:56:21.711
But even before I can alight
the steps of the mosque...

445
00:56:22.412 --> 00:56:25.313
...there is someone
to reach me home.

446
00:56:25.615 --> 00:56:27.378
Why wouldn't anyone?

447
00:56:27.851 --> 00:56:30.376
There's not a soul in town
who does not respect you.

448
00:56:30.854 --> 00:56:33.516
When they respect you so much,
why won't they help you too?

449
00:56:34.057 --> 00:56:36.525
It's all very natural.
Actually...

450
00:56:36.960 --> 00:56:39.952
When you can talk so much, why don't
you talk some sense to Ahmed too?

451
00:56:40.563 --> 00:56:42.929
He's even younger to you.

452
00:56:43.233 --> 00:56:45.565
I know how to make them
see sense, lmam.

453
00:56:46.369 --> 00:56:48.132
I can make your son
see reason too.

454
00:56:48.371 --> 00:56:54.640
But unless I know what I have
to talk about, how will I?

455
00:56:55.311 --> 00:56:59.577
Ahmed's uncle works for a beedi-
manufacturing factory in Jabalpur.

456
00:56:59.949 --> 00:57:01.883
- He earns 300 Rupees every month!
- Really?

457
00:57:02.619 --> 00:57:05.884
He has written to me so very often
to send Ahmed over...

458
00:57:06.756 --> 00:57:08.519
...so he'll talk to his boss and
find Ahmed a job in the same factory.

459
00:57:09.058 --> 00:57:11.151
But Ahmed is just not
prepared to go!

460
00:57:11.594 --> 00:57:14.154
He says I'd be left all alone!

461
00:57:14.464 --> 00:57:17.297
- Hi! How are you?
- I'm fine, all right.

462
00:57:17.634 --> 00:57:21.764
Now tell me; you've completed your
matriculation and speak English too.

463
00:57:22.138 --> 00:57:24.629
And as your uncle
in Jabalpur writes...

464
00:57:25.175 --> 00:57:27.405
There you are! You're taken up
with my father says, too!

465
00:57:27.610 --> 00:57:29.373
That's the only thing he says
to anyone who meets him.

466
00:57:29.746 --> 00:57:32.146
So what's wrong? I just answered
a question she asked.

467
00:57:32.515 --> 00:57:34.506
You know, I'm not used
to talking without reason.

468
00:57:34.851 --> 00:57:38.150
But just think it over!
It's a beedi-manufacturing factory!

469
00:57:38.455 --> 00:57:40.946
Work while you work... and smoke
a beedi, when you feel like it!

470
00:57:41.224 --> 00:57:44.625
It's like getting all the
mangoes for nothing...

471
00:57:45.128 --> 00:57:47.323
- My God!
- What's wrong??

472
00:57:48.164 --> 00:57:50.928
The mangoes! I forgot them again!

473
00:57:51.267 --> 00:57:52.632
- The raw-mangoes!
- The raw mangoes?

474
00:57:52.769 --> 00:57:54.566
Yes. I had to fetch them
for the pickle...

475
00:58:17.527 --> 00:58:19.893
Well? What are you doing here?

476
00:58:20.363 --> 00:58:22.695
Well...! That's how it is.

477
00:58:23.366 --> 00:58:25.960
Well... which mango do you
want me to knock off?

478
00:58:26.369 --> 00:58:28.701
Can you really shoot down
the mango I want?

479
00:58:29.072 --> 00:58:30.664
That's child's play!

480
00:58:30.740 --> 00:58:33.675
The best of the big shots pay
respects at my meet...

481
00:58:34.344 --> 00:58:36.835
...and swear they haven't seen
a marksman like me!

482
00:58:37.347 --> 00:58:39.247
You seem to be a damn good-shot!

483
00:58:39.616 --> 00:58:41.982
Sure... he's of royal
descent, isn't he?

484
00:58:42.385 --> 00:58:46.344
- What was that he said?
- Never mind. He talks nonsense.

485
00:58:46.623 --> 00:58:47.988
So, which mango do you want?

486
00:58:50.226 --> 00:58:53.753
That one there... the other one,
too. And yet another one there.

487
00:59:06.576 --> 00:59:08.942
My word! Your friend
is a great shot, too!

488
00:59:09.279 --> 00:59:10.746
Eh? Oh, yes. Bright chap, you know.

489
00:59:11.147 --> 00:59:13.547
I'm still teaching him...
He'll learn soon.

490
00:59:14.250 --> 00:59:17.117
- Can you teach me, too?
- Certainly! I can teach you, too!

491
00:59:17.587 --> 00:59:19.953
In fact, I can teach you this
in a matter of two days.

492
00:59:20.823 --> 00:59:22.450
- In just two days?!
- Of course.

493
00:59:22.926 --> 00:59:25.486
There have been people he has
"taught" in a couple of hours!

494
00:59:29.032 --> 00:59:31.728
- In just a couple of hours!
- He talks nonsense, you know!

495
00:59:31.968 --> 00:59:34.801
Well, come with me, if you
wish to learn this.

496
00:59:35.271 --> 00:59:37.364
Can you see that mango there?

497
00:59:37.740 --> 00:59:39.640
- You can see it, can't you?
- Sure.

498
00:59:40.009 --> 00:59:41.636
Now hold the gun...

499
00:59:42.045 --> 00:59:47.915
...and bring this other hand...
close to the other.

500
00:59:49.185 --> 00:59:52.120
Now place this finger
on the trigger.

501
00:59:53.256 --> 00:59:54.655
Now close your eye and...

502
00:59:55.158 --> 00:59:58.093
I have already shut my eyes!

503
00:59:58.761 --> 01:00:01.025
What is he talking about?

504
01:00:01.331 --> 01:00:02.662
The usual nonsense!

505
01:00:03.066 --> 01:00:05.534
- Now close your eyes.
- Very well.

506
01:00:06.502 --> 01:00:09.801
You've shut your eyes, have you?
Now... can you see that mango?

507
01:00:11.741 --> 01:00:15.233
Strange! How can I see the mango,
when I've shut my eyes?

508
01:00:16.145 --> 01:00:17.806
- Have you shut both your eyes?!
- Yes.

509
01:00:18.548 --> 01:00:20.379
But you must shut only
your left eye... this one!

510
01:00:21.851 --> 01:00:24.149
Now use your other eye
to aim at the mango.

511
01:00:25.221 --> 01:00:28.054
- Okay. And what do I do now?
- Now? Well...

512
01:00:28.625 --> 01:00:30.525
Now squeeze the trigger!

513
01:00:35.798 --> 01:00:37.527
He's found his mark!

514
01:00:38.468 --> 01:00:41.995
I thought I was learning
to handle a gun.

515
01:00:42.472 --> 01:00:45.100
But now I smell a rat!

516
01:00:45.675 --> 01:00:49.304
A rat? What is that?
I don't understand!

517
01:00:49.779 --> 01:00:51.269
But I understand this
perfectly well!

518
01:00:51.714 --> 01:00:55.445
You city-guys think we in the
countryside are morons!

519
01:00:55.752 --> 01:01:01.384
But Basanti could very well
teach you a lesson!

520
01:01:02.358 --> 01:01:06.021
I was only teaching you!
You're misunderstanding me!

521
01:01:06.429 --> 01:01:09.057
I understand you very well!

522
01:01:09.666 --> 01:01:12.931
Sit here with your gun!
I'm going home!

523
01:01:13.569 --> 01:01:15.093
Good-bye!

524
01:04:00.536 --> 01:04:04.734
Kashiram! Dholiya!
Where the hell are all of you?

525
01:04:11.347 --> 01:04:14.646
Come, Shankar...
what have you brought?

526
01:04:15.418 --> 01:04:17.352
It's some jowar, sir.

527
01:04:17.920 --> 01:04:22.050
Bloody fiend! You give us
a handful of jowar?

528
01:04:22.592 --> 01:04:25.720
D'you want to feed the guests at your
daughter's wedding with the rest?

529
01:04:26.462 --> 01:04:28.487
I speak the truth, sir!
I've brought all I had!

530
01:04:29.165 --> 01:04:34.432
We need just one bullet
to blow your brains out!

531
01:04:35.004 --> 01:04:36.528
The stinking bastard!

532
01:04:41.010 --> 01:04:42.409
And what have you got, Dholiya?

533
01:04:42.745 --> 01:04:44.212
It's wheat, sir.

534
01:04:44.847 --> 01:04:47.907
Very well. Keep all the stuff there.

535
01:04:48.484 --> 01:04:50.418
Hold it.

536
01:04:51.153 --> 01:04:53.053
Welcome, Thakur!

537
01:04:54.523 --> 01:04:56.320
You're still alive, are you?

538
01:04:57.293 --> 01:05:00.751
Yes. And till such time
as I live...

539
01:05:01.530 --> 01:05:05.261
...tell Gabbar you won't even
get a grain from this village.

540
01:05:06.469 --> 01:05:08.733
And who's going to stop us? You?

541
01:05:09.405 --> 01:05:14.638
es. My men and I will.

542
01:05:16.512 --> 01:05:18.446
These men?

543
01:05:19.815 --> 01:05:23.683
HHeard that, guys? The Thakur has
built an army of eunuchs!

544
01:05:24.754 --> 01:05:27.951
Death hovers over
your head, Kalia!

545
01:05:28.391 --> 01:05:30.655
Just look around!

546
01:05:46.475 --> 01:05:48.943
Two of them? Is that all?

547
01:05:49.512 --> 01:05:51.343
That's enough for you.

548
01:05:52.448 --> 01:05:55.417
Kashiram... have all
the things taken back.

549
01:05:56.452 --> 01:05:58.147
Think it over, Thakur.

550
01:05:58.654 --> 01:06:00.417
When Gabbar gets to know...

551
01:06:00.923 --> 01:06:04.086
...that people of this village
refuse to give him foodgrains...

552
01:06:04.860 --> 01:06:06.623
...there can be a lot
of bloodshed.

553
01:06:07.530 --> 01:06:09.555
Why must you simply...

554
01:06:18.107 --> 01:06:19.699
Get lost!

555
01:06:20.242 --> 01:06:22.267
And tell Gabbar...

556
01:06:22.778 --> 01:06:27.112
...that the people of Ramgarh
have stopped feeding mad dogs!

557
01:06:28.517 --> 01:06:30.610
Go away!

558
01:06:31.153 --> 01:06:35.055
All righn, Thakur!
I will go away!

559
01:07:24.707 --> 01:07:26.766
How many were they?

560
01:07:27.676 --> 01:07:30.110
There were two of them, chief.

561
01:07:38.487 --> 01:07:40.421
Two of them?

562
01:07:40.823 --> 01:07:42.256
Goddamned bastards!

563
01:07:46.996 --> 01:07:50.124
here were just two of them...
and there were three of you.

564
01:07:52.301 --> 01:07:55.702
You have still returned...

565
01:07:57.940 --> 01:07:59.771
...without anything.

566
01:08:01.477 --> 01:08:03.502
What did you expect?

567
01:08:04.713 --> 01:08:06.681
That I'd be delighted?!

568
01:08:07.950 --> 01:08:10.043
That I'd congratulate you?!

569
01:08:12.421 --> 01:08:14.184
Shame on you!

570
01:08:20.229 --> 01:08:21.821
Samba!

571
01:08:22.331 --> 01:08:24.595
What prize has the Government
placed on my head?

572
01:08:24.667 --> 01:08:27.033
Fifty thousand Rupees, no less.

573
01:08:27.470 --> 01:08:29.199
Did you hear him?

574
01:08:30.439 --> 01:08:33.033
Fifty grand!

575
01:08:34.610 --> 01:08:37.010
And that's only because...

576
01:08:38.013 --> 01:08:41.449
...when children as many as
50 miles away from here...

577
01:08:42.451 --> 01:08:44.612
...when the babies are hollering
away in the nights...

578
01:08:45.187 --> 01:08:50.181
....their mother ask them to go to
sleep, lest Gabbar Singh arrives!

579
01:08:52.528 --> 01:08:54.155
And these bastards!

580
01:08:54.497 --> 01:08:58.228
They've done my reputation to dust!

581
01:09:01.203 --> 01:09:05.333
You will be punished.
You certainly will!

582
01:09:12.982 --> 01:09:14.381
How many bullets does
this gun have?

583
01:09:14.850 --> 01:09:16.977
- How many bullets in this?
- There are six, chief.

584
01:09:20.222 --> 01:09:21.416
Six bullets.

585
01:09:23.792 --> 01:09:25.783
This gun has six bullets.

586
01:09:28.097 --> 01:09:32.397
Six bullets... for just 3 men.

587
01:09:33.235 --> 01:09:35.567
That's an injustice!

588
01:09:41.277 --> 01:09:45.179
It's okay now... it certainly is.

589
01:09:47.850 --> 01:09:52.344
Three parts of this now hold
bullets; and three are empty.

590
01:09:53.789 --> 01:09:56.815
I'll just roll the
whole stuff over.

591
01:10:00.362 --> 01:10:05.766
I don't know now where the bullets
are, or where they are not.

592
01:10:06.669 --> 01:10:09.433
I know nothing!

593
01:10:13.809 --> 01:10:22.547
This gun now holds three lives
and three deaths.

594
01:10:23.953 --> 01:10:27.411
Let's see what they get.

595
01:10:34.263 --> 01:10:36.197
He's escaped!

596
01:10:53.882 --> 01:10:56.180
He's escaped, too!

597
01:11:04.460 --> 01:11:07.327
What's gonna happen
of you, Kaliya?

598
01:11:07.863 --> 01:11:11.128
Chief! I've always lived
on what I got from you!

599
01:11:13.335 --> 01:11:17.271
ln's nime you snopped a bullen.

600
01:11:24.813 --> 01:11:26.246
This is amazing!

601
01:11:39.328 --> 01:11:41.353
All three have escaped!

602
01:11:41.764 --> 01:11:46.565
None of the bastards
stopped a bullet!

603
01:12:13.595 --> 01:12:15.426
All three have escaped!

604
01:13:05.914 --> 01:13:10.942
Death to the cowards!

605
01:13:24.199 --> 01:13:26.099
When is the festival of colours?
When is Holi?

606
01:22:44.359 --> 01:22:49.023
Well... so this is the
Thakur's soldier!

607
01:22:52.400 --> 01:22:57.133
Kaliya told us there
were two of them, Samba.

608
01:22:58.673 --> 01:23:00.698
Where is the other?

609
01:23:01.142 --> 01:23:03.610
Where are you, soldier?!

610
01:23:05.246 --> 01:23:09.182
Hey, soldier... where
is your partner?

611
01:23:09.484 --> 01:23:10.917
Speak up!

612
01:23:11.152 --> 01:23:13.143
Listen, you other soldier!

613
01:23:13.722 --> 01:23:17.556
Will you step out, or do
I gun down your friend here?

614
01:23:17.625 --> 01:23:19.217
Hold it!

615
01:23:21.696 --> 01:23:26.292
Welcome...! Welcome!

616
01:23:28.837 --> 01:23:31.601
We now have you in
our clutches!

617
01:23:34.075 --> 01:23:35.235
Welcome...

618
01:23:38.146 --> 01:23:40.637
Good-boy!

619
01:23:54.662 --> 01:24:00.794
Well, Thakur? You broughn nhese guys
to protect Ramgarh, did you?

620
01:24:01.269 --> 01:24:03.237
To take on Gabbar, did you?

621
01:24:03.805 --> 01:24:05.329
Listen, you villagers!

622
01:24:05.907 --> 01:24:08.967
Take a look out here!

623
01:24:09.611 --> 01:24:12.808
These the guys who came here
to protect you from me!

624
01:24:14.249 --> 01:24:18.208
Have they lost your pluck?
All of it?!

625
01:24:22.690 --> 01:24:27.457
There's only one man who can
save you from Gabbar's wrath!

626
01:24:29.030 --> 01:24:30.895
And that's Gabbar himself!

627
01:24:32.434 --> 01:24:37.531
In exchange for your security, if
we take some provisions from you....

628
01:24:38.306 --> 01:24:40.433
...that is no crime or injustice!

629
01:24:40.809 --> 01:24:43.801
No crime, I say!
It's no injustice!

630
01:24:45.447 --> 01:24:52.819
That's it then! Should anyone
dare raise his head again...

631
01:24:53.221 --> 01:24:55.348
...I will...

632
01:25:00.895 --> 01:25:02.760
The heads!

633
01:25:03.465 --> 01:25:06.457
You think these guys are
accomplished fighters, don't you?

634
01:25:07.402 --> 01:25:09.495
These hired-gunmen will now...

635
01:25:10.004 --> 01:25:15.943
...place their heads on my feet
and beg for mercy!

636
01:25:18.179 --> 01:25:20.409
They will beg at my feet!

637
01:25:24.853 --> 01:25:28.345
You've heard me, haven't you?
You have?

638
01:25:31.059 --> 01:25:34.859
Those heads of yours...
at my feet!

639
01:25:36.998 --> 01:25:38.556
Come on.

640
01:25:39.467 --> 01:25:40.934
Move, I say!

641
01:26:14.169 --> 01:26:16.069
Hurry up, Dhanno!

642
01:28:05.980 --> 01:28:10.144
We can't wage this battle
for you anymore, Thakur!

643
01:28:10.985 --> 01:28:14.751
We held you in great respect.
But it's all over!

644
01:28:15.623 --> 01:28:18.353
We came here for
the brave inspector...

645
01:28:18.726 --> 01:28:22.492
...who waged a lone battle against
a gang of bandits in the train.

646
01:28:23.164 --> 01:28:24.791
We didy'n come here
for a coward...

647
01:28:25.199 --> 01:28:29.465
...who couldn't pick up a gun lying
before him to save our lives!

648
01:28:31.372 --> 01:28:34.603
It's okay, if you wish to leave.

649
01:28:35.176 --> 01:28:36.666
You can go.

650
01:28:37.345 --> 01:28:42.647
Before you leave, won't you
want to know the reason...

651
01:28:43.985 --> 01:28:45.646
...why I didn't pick up
this gun lying here?

652
01:28:45.720 --> 01:28:50.521
What reason can there be?
You're a coward!

653
01:28:54.329 --> 01:28:58.766
It's a long story.

654
01:28:58.833 --> 01:29:03.065
It happened during the days I was
posted at the Belapur police station.

655
01:29:03.905 --> 01:29:08.865
We got information that Gabbar was
going to loot the village Haripur.

656
01:29:09.711 --> 01:29:10.871
The police raided them
at the right time...

657
01:29:10.978 --> 01:29:13.572
...and the bandits had to flee.

658
01:29:14.115 --> 01:29:17.448
I started chasing Gabbar.

659
01:31:21.008 --> 01:31:25.604
Let me go... let go...
Leave me alone, you bastard!

660
01:31:26.514 --> 01:31:31.110
Gabbar Singh! This is no arm!
This is a noose!

661
01:31:33.087 --> 01:31:35.715
In view of the testimonies
and the evidence at hand...

662
01:31:36.057 --> 01:31:37.820
....this Court reaches
the conclusion that...

663
01:31:38.125 --> 01:31:42.323
...Gabbar Singh is a dangerous
and professional criminal.

664
01:31:42.730 --> 01:31:45.995
This court, therefore, holding
him guilty of dacoity...

665
01:31:46.367 --> 01:31:51.896
...sentences him to 20 years
of rigorous imprisonment.

666
01:31:57.278 --> 01:32:01.738
I'll remember you...
I'm sure, I will remember you.

667
01:32:02.517 --> 01:32:07.250
After 20 years in the prison,
you will forget everything, Gabbar.

668
01:32:07.755 --> 01:32:10.622
No prison in the world
has walls strong enough...

669
01:32:10.992 --> 01:32:13.927
...to hold Gabbar captive
for 20 long years.

670
01:32:15.263 --> 01:32:21.031
And the day I escape...
you will regret it, Thakur.

671
01:32:22.136 --> 01:32:24.536
You're going to regret it.

672
01:32:24.605 --> 01:32:25.867
Take him away.

673
01:32:25.940 --> 01:32:31.674
TThis enmity's going to
cost you dear, Thakur!

674
01:32:33.614 --> 01:32:36.412
Thakur! Congratulations!

675
01:32:37.018 --> 01:32:39.714
Another criminal you've nabbed
is coming to my prison.

676
01:32:41.522 --> 01:32:45.515
He's a dangerous man, jailer.
You'd better be careful.

677
01:32:47.028 --> 01:32:49.588
I'm glad your application
for leave has come through.

678
01:32:50.031 --> 01:32:52.966
It had to anyway. You're going on
leave after a very long time.

679
01:32:53.367 --> 01:32:58.270
Had I not taken leave now, my folks
would have stopped talking to me.

680
01:32:58.606 --> 01:33:01.541
It's the same story with
everyone in our profession.

681
01:33:01.943 --> 01:33:03.740
I face the same problem.

682
01:33:04.145 --> 01:33:05.908
How many members do
you have in your family?

683
01:33:06.247 --> 01:33:12.049
I have two sons who are married and
a daughter of marriageable age, too.

684
01:33:12.119 --> 01:33:14.587
I want to find a nice groom
for her this time.

685
01:33:15.089 --> 01:33:16.750
I also have a grandson.

686
01:33:16.824 --> 01:33:19.088
Really? You don't look so old!

687
01:33:19.460 --> 01:33:22.486
We in the village are
married very early in life.

688
01:33:22.930 --> 01:33:25.558
An early marriage means
the son comes early, too.

689
01:33:25.933 --> 01:33:28.902
Since the son marries early,
he has a son very soon.

690
01:33:29.303 --> 01:33:30.930
In fact, he's about
8 years of age.

691
01:33:31.005 --> 01:33:34.236
Old enough to take offence if
you don't visit him on leave?

692
01:33:34.308 --> 01:33:35.570
You bet!

693
01:33:36.010 --> 01:33:39.173
I'm carrying gifts for everyone,
in order to pacify them.

694
01:33:39.614 --> 01:33:43.846
There you are then; I've never
accepted a bribe in my life.

695
01:33:44.251 --> 01:33:47.152
Bun l have no bribe my family,
wheyever l go home!

696
01:33:48.723 --> 01:33:51.123
I must take your leave now.

697
01:33:54.929 --> 01:33:57.864
- What is it?
- Gabbar Singh has escaped, sir!

698
01:33:57.932 --> 01:33:59.900
Gabbar Singh has escaped?!

699
01:34:02.670 --> 01:34:04.001
You've missed again!

700
01:34:04.338 --> 01:34:05.930
You're no good, uncle!

701
01:34:06.207 --> 01:34:09.176
Oh sure! Your father's been hunting
lions, hasn't he? Just shut up!

702
01:34:09.276 --> 01:34:12.439
You're going to the station to
receive grandpa, aren't you?

703
01:34:13.114 --> 01:34:15.014
- May I come along, too?
- Go and ask your mother.

704
01:34:15.416 --> 01:34:16.713
Why don't you tell her?

705
01:34:17.084 --> 01:34:20.918
Just tell her that you're
going with me. Go on.

706
01:34:23.124 --> 01:34:24.386
Monher...

707
01:34:25.960 --> 01:34:27.257
Len me cun nhe vegenables.

708
01:34:27.495 --> 01:34:30.225
May I go to the station
with uncle, mother?

709
01:34:30.564 --> 01:34:32.191
No. You're not going
to the station.

710
01:34:32.533 --> 01:34:36.230
Madam... I've asked someone
to fix the main-gate.

711
01:34:36.871 --> 01:34:42.741
And here are the things
you had asked for...

712
01:34:45.312 --> 01:34:49.248
- Young mistress!
- I'm coming over!

713
01:34:57.158 --> 01:35:01.219
I'm going to the temple. But if
there is anything I can do...?

714
01:35:01.662 --> 01:35:03.357
Go on. I'll handle it.

715
01:35:03.731 --> 01:35:05.062
- Let's go.
- Give me that.

716
01:35:09.170 --> 01:35:12.435
- May I go to the station, mom?
- Haven't I said you can't?

717
01:35:13.274 --> 01:35:15.435
Let him go, if he wants to.

718
01:35:15.876 --> 01:35:17.776
No way. There are always so many
trains passing by.

719
01:35:18.212 --> 01:35:19.372
I'm scared.

720
01:35:19.680 --> 01:35:22.547
The trains seem to have an axe
to grind against your son.

721
01:35:23.017 --> 01:35:25.986
They'll leave their tracks
to go after him!

722
01:35:26.954 --> 01:35:28.683
ou have a funny logic.

723
01:35:29.890 --> 01:35:32.984
So you're preparing the
vegetable father likes, eh?

724
01:35:33.794 --> 01:35:36.388
- Let him go, I say.
- Okay! Go ahead and spoil him!

725
01:35:37.698 --> 01:35:40.326
Will you go like this?
Go and have a bath.

726
01:35:40.835 --> 01:35:43.167
Ask your aunt to...
Nirmala!

727
01:35:43.237 --> 01:35:45.034
Yes, sister-in-law?

728
01:35:45.406 --> 01:35:46.930
Will you get a set of clothes
out for the kid, my girl?

729
01:35:47.007 --> 01:35:49.032
Right away.

730
01:35:49.110 --> 01:35:50.543
Go on.

731
01:35:50.611 --> 01:35:53.205
And you've started chewing
on the raw vegetables!

732
01:35:53.314 --> 01:35:57.512
They're all busy today
to impress father!

733
01:35:57.818 --> 01:36:00.651
As if you get the witch to
do the chores every day!

734
01:36:01.322 --> 01:36:04.450
This wheel is still lying here?

735
01:36:05.593 --> 01:36:09.029
Ramlal has become
a forgetful old man.

736
01:36:09.730 --> 01:36:14.497
I'd asked him to have the drawing
room and father's room cleaned.

737
01:36:14.735 --> 01:36:16.430
But he's not even to be seen.

738
01:36:16.971 --> 01:36:20.600
He's away at the temple with Radha.
He will do it when he returns.

739
01:36:21.909 --> 01:36:24.036
- Hey, Ninni!
- Yes, brother?

740
01:36:24.411 --> 01:36:27.710
Have a bath and get ready!
Aren't we going to the station?

741
01:36:28.115 --> 01:36:29.878
I'll join you in a minute!

742
01:36:32.787 --> 01:36:37.747
I can't figure out how this silly
hunter found a wife like Radha.

743
01:36:38.325 --> 01:36:41.021
It was I who asked father
to pursue the alliance.

744
01:36:41.495 --> 01:36:43.520
But does anyone even
acknowledge what I've done?

745
01:36:43.964 --> 01:36:46.364
I've found him a wife
who's one in a million!

746
01:36:46.667 --> 01:36:50.660
Or girls nowadays ask for a division
the day they are married.

747
01:36:51.138 --> 01:36:54.574
Wait and see what a great match
I find for Nimmo next.

748
01:36:58.379 --> 01:36:59.437
No!

749
01:41:44.231 --> 01:41:46.199
Gabbar?

750
01:41:49.970 --> 01:41:51.597
Yes...

751
01:43:50.958 --> 01:43:52.550
Welcome, Thakur.

752
01:43:54.027 --> 01:43:57.190
I knew for sure
that you'd come here.

753
01:44:01.969 --> 01:44:04.733
The ass struggles!

754
01:44:05.639 --> 01:44:08.164
You contemptible bastard!
God-damn scoundrel!

755
01:44:09.676 --> 01:44:13.271
Curse me as much as you wish!
To your heart's content!

756
01:44:13.981 --> 01:44:17.280
- You bastard!
- Yes! Shout some more!

757
01:44:17.918 --> 01:44:21.786
Remember? I cried the other day
and you watched the fun?

758
01:44:22.589 --> 01:44:26.525
You will cry your lungs out today...
and I will watch the fun!

759
01:44:27.828 --> 01:44:29.523
Know what, Samba?

760
01:44:30.330 --> 01:44:34.664
I was livid at the court that
day... so very furious!

761
01:44:35.869 --> 01:44:39.100
I could have wrung his neck
there and then! The bastard!

762
01:44:39.706 --> 01:44:43.369
But I couldn't help it!
I was held by four of those cops!

763
01:44:44.111 --> 01:44:46.545
Handcuffs in my hands...
my legs shackled! Remember?

764
01:44:48.982 --> 01:44:50.643
You remember that, don't you?

765
01:44:55.155 --> 01:44:57.749
Any last wish, Thakur?

766
01:45:04.431 --> 01:45:08.197
There's still a lot
of life in your arms.

767
01:45:09.002 --> 01:45:10.799
Tie him up!

768
01:45:24.551 --> 01:45:27.281
I'm not going to kill you now.

769
01:45:28.288 --> 01:45:33.624
After I'm through with you...
the world will spit on you.

770
01:45:35.329 --> 01:45:38.127
Your arms are full of life!

771
01:45:38.999 --> 01:45:42.935
His arms are strong enough
to pull down a running horse!

772
01:45:45.272 --> 01:45:48.730
Your arms are full of life!

773
01:45:49.476 --> 01:45:51.444
D'you remember what you
had once told me?

774
01:45:51.912 --> 01:45:55.473
They aren't arms...
they're a noose!

775
01:45:56.149 --> 01:46:00.051
And here you are!
The noose has been destroyed!

776
01:46:00.754 --> 01:46:02.449
It has been ripped open!

777
01:46:03.423 --> 01:46:05.687
Arms full of life, aren't they?

778
01:46:07.794 --> 01:46:09.819
These arms...

779
01:46:10.664 --> 01:46:12.188
...give them to me, Thakur.
- No!

780
01:46:13.400 --> 01:46:17.632
- Give me your arms, Thakur!
- No!

781
01:47:41.721 --> 01:47:44.155
- Did you see anything else?
- No, sir.

782
01:47:44.591 --> 01:47:47.082
We shut our doors and windows
when we heard the gunfire.

783
01:47:47.594 --> 01:47:49.960
I see... very well.

784
01:47:51.131 --> 01:47:53.691
- Put your thumb-impression here.
- Very well, sir.

785
01:47:56.303 --> 01:47:57.895
Welcome, Thakur.

786
01:48:00.373 --> 01:48:03.809
I've got to know of what happened
here, from these folks.

787
01:48:04.544 --> 01:48:05.738
I wanted to discuss
something with you.

788
01:48:06.613 --> 01:48:10.344
The police want Gabbar;
dead or alive.

789
01:48:10.984 --> 01:48:15.011
You will have him one day.

790
01:48:16.490 --> 01:48:18.890
Is there something you can
tell me about Gabbar?

791
01:48:19.893 --> 01:48:21.121
No.

792
01:48:21.795 --> 01:48:25.026
Okay. That's all I wanted to know.

793
01:48:25.098 --> 01:48:27.396
Thank you, Thakur.

794
01:48:31.137 --> 01:48:32.604
Good-bye.

795
01:48:45.385 --> 01:48:51.654
We don't want that money, Thakur.

796
01:48:52.959 --> 01:48:54.153
Please take it back.

797
01:48:55.128 --> 01:48:58.097
Please don't think, we won't carry
out the mission for you.

798
01:49:01.835 --> 01:49:06.033
But didn't you say
you only work for money?

799
01:49:06.773 --> 01:49:09.401
Well, we...

800
01:49:10.043 --> 01:49:11.977
We will get the money anyway.

801
01:49:12.779 --> 01:49:16.146
- Once we have killed Gabbar...
- You will not kill Gabbar!

802
01:49:18.585 --> 01:49:23.989
You are here to catch Gabbar alive
and hand him over to me.

803
01:49:25.158 --> 01:49:29.288
Give me your word! That you will
hand him over to me, alive!

804
01:49:35.635 --> 01:49:41.699
We give you our word, Thakur.
But please take back the money.

805
01:49:44.678 --> 01:49:47.875
Girija, the blacksmith, brings
some news from village Titli.

806
01:49:51.318 --> 01:49:55.914
You might meet Gabbar
again very soon.

807
01:49:56.289 --> 01:49:57.381
Come on.

808
01:50:01.561 --> 01:50:03.529
- Greetings, Thakur.
- Greetings.

809
01:50:04.264 --> 01:50:06.027
So what's news, Girija?

810
01:50:06.433 --> 01:50:09.266
There are some gypsies
staying at Pipri.

811
01:50:09.603 --> 01:50:11.093
Hira and his friends
are there too.

812
01:50:13.540 --> 01:50:16.566
Hira is the one who sells
arms and ammunition to Gabbar.

813
01:50:17.344 --> 01:50:20.609
Gabbar is bound to meet him
in a couple of days.

814
01:50:21.247 --> 01:50:25.911
Strike... when the iron is hot.

815
01:55:21.347 --> 01:55:23.679
My God! What happened to him?

816
01:55:24.417 --> 01:55:27.648
Don't worry. The bullet has
just grazed his arm.

817
01:55:28.288 --> 01:55:29.778
It's not a serious injury.

818
01:55:31.658 --> 01:55:34.320
We blew up almost all their
arms and explosives, Thakur...

819
01:55:34.794 --> 01:55:36.455
...but Gabbar managed to escape.

820
01:55:37.096 --> 01:55:41.089
It's okay. We'll get him
again someday.

821
01:55:45.471 --> 01:55:49.271
Take a swig, partner.
Your troubles will vanish.

822
01:55:50.710 --> 01:55:54.441
Should you stop drinking, it will
reduce most of your troubles.

823
01:55:55.448 --> 01:55:56.710
- Would you like to...?
- God almighty!

824
01:56:21.441 --> 01:56:24.604
Greetings, lmam.
I have a letter for you.

825
01:56:25.378 --> 01:56:28.176
- Here you are.
- It must be from Jabalpur.

826
01:56:28.715 --> 01:56:32.981
- Could you read it for me?
- Certainly.

827
01:56:34.620 --> 01:56:36.679
Where are my glasses?
I put it in my pocket!

828
01:56:37.023 --> 01:56:40.083
That which you are looking for
is here with me!

829
01:56:40.994 --> 01:56:42.791
- Here you are!
- The chatterbox is here, isn't she?

830
01:56:43.463 --> 01:56:46.728
Actually, we were going in
the opposite directions.

831
01:56:47.567 --> 01:56:49.797
You were on your bicycle
and I was on foot.

832
01:56:50.136 --> 01:56:52.969
You dropped your glasses
and I picked them up!

833
01:56:53.473 --> 01:56:56.169
I guessed as much that the
glasses must belong to you.

834
01:56:56.509 --> 01:56:59.239
The funny part is, it's
really yours. Actually...

835
01:57:00.146 --> 01:57:02.910
If you rest your mouth a little,
I'd know what the letter says.

836
01:57:03.349 --> 01:57:06.750
- I'll listen to you later.
- Okay! When did I refuse?

837
01:57:08.221 --> 01:57:11.349
- It begins with a greeting.
- Greetings himself, too.

838
01:57:12.225 --> 01:57:16.161
Everything is fine here and we
pray for your well-being.

839
01:57:18.598 --> 01:57:22.762
"The good news is that the job
for Ahmed has been finalized''

840
01:57:23.536 --> 01:57:25.595
"He will get a salary
of 200 Rupees''

841
01:57:25.938 --> 01:57:29.032
"He can very well stay with me
and eat with us, too''

842
01:57:29.475 --> 01:57:32.410
It's good that he will
be in his uncle's care.

843
01:57:32.745 --> 01:57:34.804
Oh yes! That's wonderful!
That's just what I wanted, too.

844
01:57:35.581 --> 01:57:38.049
"It wouldn't be proper to delay
this matter anymore''

845
01:57:38.451 --> 01:57:41.249
"I hope you will treat this
letter like a telegram''

846
01:57:41.521 --> 01:57:45.013
"Please arrange to send
Ahmed here at the earliest''

847
01:57:45.358 --> 01:57:48.486
"Everything else is fine here;
my folks send you their regards''

848
01:57:48.828 --> 01:57:52.821
- " I remain, yours...
- Mukait Ul-lah.

849
01:57:53.166 --> 01:57:55.259
I will not listen to any
excuse from Ahmed now.

850
01:57:55.601 --> 01:57:59.697
That's right.
But he's very much here.

851
01:58:00.373 --> 01:58:02.967
Let me tell you, father.
I'm not going there.

852
01:58:03.309 --> 01:58:06.801
- This is like...
- This boy is a fool!

853
01:58:07.213 --> 01:58:12.515
I have one foot in the grave and you
have your life ahead of you!

854
01:58:12.919 --> 01:58:18.016
How long will you cling to me?
You don't find such jobs everyday.

855
01:58:18.591 --> 01:58:20.650
Your father is right, son.

856
01:58:20.960 --> 01:58:27.866
In fact, I've heard of people
praying at temples in the cities...

857
01:58:28.901 --> 01:58:31.426
- The temple?!
- What's wrong?

858
01:58:31.804 --> 01:58:37.902
Actually, I was headed for the temple
and happened to find his glasses.

859
01:58:38.010 --> 01:58:41.173
That's it! I forgot
where I was going!

860
01:58:41.614 --> 01:58:44.082
But I've remembered it now!

861
01:58:46.986 --> 01:58:51.320
Hey, Veeru... nhere goes
your horse-cart girl.

862
01:58:56.562 --> 01:58:59.531
Well, Basanti...
you're on foot today.

863
01:58:59.966 --> 01:59:02.764
Has your mare run away
with the cart?

864
01:59:03.202 --> 01:59:09.766
You still don't understand
that no one elopes out here.

865
01:59:10.109 --> 01:59:13.340
My mare is honorably at home
and today being a Monday...

866
01:59:13.713 --> 01:59:17.706
...aunt told me that if I pray
to Lord Shiva on every Monday...

867
01:59:19.085 --> 01:59:21.451
...l'll get a husband that
the world will be stunned.

868
01:59:21.921 --> 01:59:26.153
I said, okay... I don't intend
to marry a bum anyway.

869
01:59:26.592 --> 01:59:29.152
Okay, then... I must leave.
Praise the Lord!

870
01:59:34.700 --> 01:59:36.861
Praise the Lord!

871
01:59:41.574 --> 01:59:43.098
Praise the Lord!

872
02:00:01.460 --> 02:00:06.193
Lord! There is nothing in the
world that is hidden from You.

873
02:00:06.599 --> 02:00:08.590
You are omniscient, Lord!

874
02:00:08.968 --> 02:00:11.232
I don't say that You have
forgotten it.

875
02:00:11.604 --> 02:00:13.936
But it's always good
to remind You.

876
02:00:14.307 --> 02:00:17.572
Today's a Monday and I have
a small request, Lord.

877
02:00:17.977 --> 02:00:24.712
Look at my hands, rough and rugged
from holding the reins!

878
02:00:25.318 --> 02:00:27.013
And what problems
could You have, Lord?

879
02:00:27.086 --> 02:00:31.989
Get me married into a family where
I will rule like the Queens!

880
02:00:32.425 --> 02:00:34.325
Life's gotta be fun!

881
02:00:35.027 --> 02:00:39.020
I leave the rest to You.

882
02:00:39.565 --> 02:00:41.089
Young lady...

883
02:00:42.802 --> 02:00:44.895
Who spoke?

884
02:00:46.072 --> 02:00:48.905
It is I who has spoken!

885
02:00:49.709 --> 02:00:53.543
Lord! It's You!
This is a miracle!

886
02:00:56.949 --> 02:01:02.012
l have fouyd a manch
foryou, lady.

887
02:01:02.655 --> 02:01:05.385
In just one Monday?
That's excellent!

888
02:01:05.758 --> 02:01:07.953
You must obviously have
chosen the best!

889
02:01:08.361 --> 02:01:09.328
Could You tell me the name, perhaps?
Or do I come again next week?

890
02:01:11.998 --> 02:01:13.625
I will do as You say, Lord.

891
02:01:13.699 --> 02:01:16.793
His name is Veeru.

892
02:01:26.345 --> 02:01:29.337
He's okay to look at;
but he's a bloody smart ass!

893
02:01:29.782 --> 02:01:31.943
Silence, maiden!

894
02:01:32.285 --> 02:01:36.016
I never talk without reason, Lord!
I'll do as You say!

895
02:01:36.622 --> 02:01:43.687
lf you doy'n obey my commayd, you
will remaiy a spiysner all your life!

896
02:01:43.796 --> 02:01:45.627
Forgive me, Lord!

897
02:01:48.434 --> 02:01:52.165
You will continue to drive the
horse-cart all your life!

898
02:01:52.805 --> 02:01:59.643
I now command you to go and tell
your aunt, in no uncertain terms...

899
02:02:00.813 --> 02:02:05.147
...that it is Veeru who will be
your companion for life!

900
02:02:06.085 --> 02:02:11.421
To respect and honor Veeru therefore
shall be your prime duty!

901
02:02:12.325 --> 02:02:17.058
Because, your heavens
lie at his feet!

902
02:02:17.997 --> 02:02:23.060
Should you please him,
I shall be pleased!

903
02:02:23.736 --> 02:02:29.436
And if you irritate him,
I shall be enraged!

904
02:02:29.709 --> 02:02:31.370
Really?

905
02:02:31.977 --> 02:02:33.945
So go to him...

906
02:02:49.862 --> 02:02:52.660
I thought I would...

907
02:02:53.032 --> 02:02:56.866
You thought this village belle
has no brains!

908
02:02:57.203 --> 02:02:58.761
You thought you could fool me!

909
02:02:59.105 --> 02:03:00.595
You think you're smart!

910
02:03:00.940 --> 02:03:03.807
But I could outsmart guys
like you!

911
02:03:04.110 --> 02:03:07.341
Sin here and play God!
I'm going home!

912
02:03:08.748 --> 02:03:10.978
At least listen to me!

913
02:07:23.135 --> 02:07:25.399
I've thought of
something today.

914
02:07:25.871 --> 02:07:28.499
You must do that,
once in a while.

915
02:07:29.208 --> 02:07:31.642
I've taken a very
crucial decision today.

916
02:07:32.244 --> 02:07:37.204
I know what your decision is;
you want to marry Basanti.

917
02:07:37.583 --> 02:07:40.609
That's wonderful!
You're a true friend!

918
02:07:40.953 --> 02:07:42.716
Only a friend could
know how I feel!

919
02:07:43.088 --> 02:07:48.492
But I also know that this is your
8th decision to marry this year.

920
02:07:48.894 --> 02:07:50.384
But this is final!

921
02:07:50.929 --> 02:07:53.921
Really? No wonder... you've been
drinking from early this morning.

922
02:07:55.868 --> 02:07:58.928
- Will you do something for me?
- What is it?

923
02:07:59.371 --> 02:08:03.967
Go and talk to Basanti's aunt;
make such an impression...

924
02:08:04.076 --> 02:08:05.941
...that the old lady is compelled
to propose our marriage!

925
02:08:06.278 --> 02:08:07.540
Why must I do that?

926
02:08:08.380 --> 02:08:10.109
Naturally! It's the groom's folks
who approach the bride's parents!

927
02:08:10.549 --> 02:08:14.212
Besides, you're the only one
I have in the world, my friend!

928
02:08:14.553 --> 02:08:17.181
It's your wedding, okay?
So go and do this yourself.

929
02:08:18.290 --> 02:08:22.056
Give it a thought...
a cozy home, after marriage!

930
02:08:22.528 --> 02:08:25.156
- A home that is yours.
- A loving wife...

931
02:08:25.264 --> 02:08:27.289
- Your wife.
- A handful of kids...

932
02:08:27.399 --> 02:08:30.596
- All yours, too.
- You're the one they'll call uncle!

933
02:08:31.070 --> 02:08:33.937
They'll forever pester you,
play with you all the time...

934
02:08:34.473 --> 02:08:39.740
...and ask you
to tell them a story!

935
02:08:41.814 --> 02:08:46.478
Which means I'm going to play
the maid-servant in your house.

936
02:08:46.952 --> 02:08:50.353
It's clear now!
You are no friend!

937
02:08:51.156 --> 02:08:52.453
To hell with such a...

938
02:08:57.663 --> 02:09:01.895
Acting pricey, aren't you? Because
no one else can do this for me?

939
02:09:04.436 --> 02:09:07.837
Had only my mom been alive,
I'd have settled down in life!

940
02:09:08.373 --> 02:09:09.806
I'd even have had kids!

941
02:09:10.209 --> 02:09:14.145
Had my old man been around, he'd
have celebrated my wedding in style!

942
02:09:14.646 --> 02:09:17.979
Had I brothers and sisters, they'd
have begged the old lady...

943
02:09:18.050 --> 02:09:20.109
...but seen to it that
I married Basanti.

944
02:09:20.686 --> 02:09:25.248
ut don't you forget! Those without
support, have God on their side!

945
02:09:26.291 --> 02:09:27.417
Lord Almighty!

946
02:09:28.927 --> 02:09:30.656
You're not the friend I knew!

947
02:09:31.697 --> 02:09:34.495
You don't want me to give up crime
and settle down in life!

948
02:09:35.134 --> 02:09:41.334
What had I imagined you to be...
and what you really are!

949
02:09:45.677 --> 02:09:49.374
The bloody clown...
he's forever up to dramatics!

950
02:09:52.551 --> 02:09:55.987
Cut the act! I'll go and talk
it over with the old lady.

951
02:09:56.455 --> 02:09:57.149
Will you, really?!

952
02:09:57.923 --> 02:10:04.328
An unmarried girl at home is
like a burden on the soul, son.

953
02:10:04.863 --> 02:10:08.321
I can be at peace, only when
Basanti is married.

954
02:10:08.734 --> 02:10:13.398
You're right. You are indeed
bearing a burden.

955
02:10:14.006 --> 02:10:17.237
But I can't just dump her
in a well, can I?

956
02:10:17.643 --> 02:10:21.306
Please don't mind this,
but I must ask...

957
02:10:22.481 --> 02:10:27.384
...about the suitor's family,
his habits and his earnings.

958
02:10:28.420 --> 02:10:33.221
As far as earnings go,
once he is married,

959
02:10:34.426 --> 02:10:36.724
...he will start earning
to fend for them.

960
02:10:37.396 --> 02:10:40.524
Doesn't he earning anything
at the moment, then?

961
02:10:41.166 --> 02:10:43.600
Of course, he does!
When did I say that he doesn't?

962
02:10:44.303 --> 02:10:47.534
It's like this; no one can
win all the time, can he?

963
02:10:48.407 --> 02:10:51.035
There are times the poor chap
even loses money.

964
02:10:51.476 --> 02:10:53.706
- Loses money?
- That's right...

965
02:10:53.979 --> 02:10:56.675
...but that's gambling, you know.
There's little I can say about it.

966
02:10:57.216 --> 02:10:59.741
My God! Is he a gambler?

967
02:11:00.085 --> 02:11:03.248
Not at all, madam!
It's a shame to call him a gambler!

968
02:11:03.689 --> 02:11:06.556
He's a gem of a person;
decent and straight.

969
02:11:06.859 --> 02:11:12.661
But when someone is high on liquor,
he can't see things in perspective.

970
02:11:12.731 --> 02:11:17.259
They force him into gambling.
How's poor Veeru to blame?

971
02:11:17.836 --> 02:11:24.867
You're right, son. A drinker and
a gambler... and yet, faultless!

972
02:11:24.943 --> 02:11:29.937
You're misunderstanding my friend.
He's an innocent, young chap.

973
02:11:31.183 --> 02:11:33.549
Just get him married to Basanti...

974
02:11:33.986 --> 02:11:37.012
...he'll give up drinking
and gambling in no time!

975
02:11:37.522 --> 02:11:39.888
Don't tell me, son.
I know better.

976
02:11:40.559 --> 02:11:43.528
Has anyone ever been able to kick
habits like drinking and gambling?

977
02:11:44.096 --> 02:11:48.396
You don't know Veeru. Believe me,
he's not at all like that.

978
02:11:48.867 --> 02:11:51.995
Once he's married, he'll stop
visiting the nautch girl. Period!

979
02:11:52.871 --> 02:11:53.997
His drinking problem will be
solved on its own!

980
02:11:54.072 --> 02:11:59.339
Good Lord! That's all he lacked!
He even visits brothels, does he?

981
02:11:59.678 --> 02:12:01.475
So what's wrong with that?

982
02:12:01.780 --> 02:12:06.717
Even kings and princes have
often patronized dancing-girls!

983
02:12:07.286 --> 02:12:13.054
I see... but can you tell me which
family your friend hails from?

984
02:12:13.492 --> 02:12:15.983
We'll let you know that,
the moment we get to know of it!

985
02:12:16.795 --> 02:12:21.357
I must say one thing, son.
For all your friend's vices...

986
02:12:22.834 --> 02:12:27.032
...you can only praise him!

987
02:12:27.539 --> 02:12:30.804
I can't help it, aunt.
I'm really soft at heart.

988
02:12:32.444 --> 02:12:35.208
So, do I take it then that
they will soon be married?

989
02:12:35.547 --> 02:12:38.983
Married? It's okay even if she
remains a spinster all her life!

990
02:12:39.318 --> 02:12:41.718
But I will not let Basanti
marry such a man!

991
02:12:41.787 --> 02:12:44.847
I'm her aunt; not her step-mother!

992
02:12:46.024 --> 02:12:51.087
It's strange that you refuse,
despite the best of my efforts.

993
02:12:52.297 --> 02:12:57.735
Poor Veeru. I don't know
how he will deal with this.

994
02:12:58.870 --> 02:13:04.308
I'll take a jump and die!
Out of my way!

995
02:13:05.344 --> 02:13:07.073
Hey, watch it!
What are you doing?

996
02:13:07.379 --> 02:13:11.315
I'm doing just what every
legendary lover has done!

997
02:13:13.852 --> 02:13:18.255
They died for their beloved's!

998
02:13:18.323 --> 02:13:23.056
Suicide!

999
02:13:23.762 --> 02:13:26.492
Well now... what is suicide?

1000
02:13:26.932 --> 02:13:29.696
Well now... what is suicide.

1001
02:13:30.202 --> 02:13:32.864
But why do the English die?

1002
02:13:33.405 --> 02:13:38.502
What's up, feller? Why do you
want to commit suicide?

1003
02:13:38.844 --> 02:13:43.338
You'd rather not ask!
You'll break into tears!

1004
02:13:43.749 --> 02:13:46.547
It's a very sad story!

1005
02:13:46.985 --> 02:13:51.581
It has emotions, drama
and tragedy!

1006
02:13:51.990 --> 02:13:56.950
You know Basanti, don't you?
I was going to marry her.

1007
02:13:57.796 --> 02:14:02.893
But her wicked aunt has
been an obstacle!

1008
02:14:03.335 --> 02:14:06.634
I can't live in this big,
bad world, anymore!

1009
02:14:06.972 --> 02:14:13.400
I bid you farewell, villagers!
Good-bye!

1010
02:14:16.915 --> 02:14:19.383
Well... what is "good-bye" ?

1011
02:14:19.751 --> 02:14:22.413
When the English leave,
it's called "good-bye"'.

1012
02:14:22.821 --> 02:14:24.982
But where do the English go?

1013
02:14:25.357 --> 02:14:28.724
Hey, villagers! Here I go!

1014
02:14:29.261 --> 02:14:31.923
God Almighty! Here I come!

1015
02:14:32.764 --> 02:14:33.958
Hold it! Wait...!

1016
02:14:34.633 --> 02:14:41.004
What?! Okay, if you insist,
I'll wait for a while.

1017
02:14:41.306 --> 02:14:45.037
Hey... you're a strange friend!
You're sitting here unaffected!

1018
02:14:45.577 --> 02:14:47.807
- Why? What's wrong?
- How am I to know?

1019
02:14:48.246 --> 02:14:50.942
Look at your friend!
He's climbed all the way up there!

1020
02:14:53.218 --> 02:14:55.118
You see that, don't you?!

1021
02:14:56.088 --> 02:14:58.716
Yes, I do.
But nothing's going to happen.

1022
02:14:59.057 --> 02:15:01.787
He'll climb down,
when he sobers down.

1023
02:15:02.994 --> 02:15:06.122
I've seen many cruel people.
But not a heartless friend like you!

1024
02:15:07.566 --> 02:15:09.033
Hey, watch out!

1025
02:15:09.734 --> 02:15:13.932
I have no one in the world!
Nor friend, nor buddy...

1026
02:15:14.272 --> 02:15:17.332
So I'm going to end my life!

1027
02:15:17.809 --> 02:15:20.676
But I must warn you, villagers!

1028
02:15:21.046 --> 02:15:27.474
Where a lover ends his life, the
village is wrought with calamities!

1029
02:15:27.619 --> 02:15:29.849
What calamities will
we have to face?

1030
02:15:29.921 --> 02:15:36.622
There will be famine and drought!
Diseases and death!

1031
02:15:37.095 --> 02:15:42.294
And all that only for the sake of
that old hag! That old hag indeed!

1032
02:15:42.400 --> 02:15:43.594
My God!

1033
02:15:43.935 --> 02:15:48.770
You will see for yourselves!
When I die...

1034
02:15:49.541 --> 02:15:54.604
...the police will arrive and take
the old hag away to jail!

1035
02:15:55.914 --> 02:16:02.786
In jail, the old hag will
labor on the grindstone...!

1036
02:16:04.222 --> 02:16:07.419
You'd better agree, lady.
Or he'll kill himself!

1037
02:16:07.859 --> 02:16:09.918
But how can I agree, Dinanath?!

1038
02:16:10.428 --> 02:16:15.957
You don't have to beg for anything
from the hag, villagers!

1039
02:16:16.401 --> 02:16:18.494
Nothing can stop me now!

1040
02:16:18.837 --> 02:16:21.670
I will certainly end my life!

1041
02:16:23.441 --> 02:16:26.740
Here goes; one, two, three...

1042
02:16:27.012 --> 02:16:28.877
Please, aunt! Agree to what he says!

1043
02:16:28.947 --> 02:16:31.313
You'd better agree, or do the rounds
of the courts and police stations!

1044
02:16:31.383 --> 02:16:33.476
But I've never been a court
or a police station!

1045
02:16:33.552 --> 02:16:35.679
- Then you'd better agree.
- All right.

1046
02:16:35.820 --> 02:16:39.654
Stop that, Veeru!
I agree!

1047
02:16:40.659 --> 02:16:43.651
The old lady has agreed!
Now quietly come down!

1048
02:16:45.096 --> 02:16:47.929
Who wants to marry
the old lady!

1049
02:16:48.266 --> 02:16:52.134
It's Dhanno... I mean,
it's Basanti I want to marry.

1050
02:16:52.704 --> 02:16:56.663
I'm willing to marry you, Veeru!
Come down now!

1051
02:16:58.176 --> 02:17:00.736
Hear that, villagers?

1052
02:17:01.246 --> 02:17:04.272
The old lady is willing...
and so is Basanti!

1053
02:17:05.050 --> 02:17:07.644
So my death has been cancelled!

1054
02:17:08.353 --> 02:17:11.345
I'm coming down, aunt...
my adorable aunt!

1055
02:17:11.423 --> 02:17:13.914
I'm coming down...

1056
02:17:18.830 --> 02:17:21.162
What am I going to do now?!

1057
02:17:40.285 --> 02:17:42.685
- So long, father.
- You're leaving, are you?

1058
02:17:43.021 --> 02:17:45.046
Go on... my God protect you.

1059
02:17:45.490 --> 02:17:48.584
Write to me, the moment
you reach there.

1060
02:17:48.927 --> 02:17:53.387
You're a very careless eater;
look after your health, okay?

1061
02:17:53.965 --> 02:17:57.366
As my father, God bless his soul,
used to say...

1062
02:17:57.836 --> 02:18:01.738
...in good health lies
true happiness and wealth.

1063
02:18:02.340 --> 02:18:05.741
Let me walk with you for a while.
I'll get myself some air, too.

1064
02:18:06.011 --> 02:18:09.447
It's okay, father. Relax...
I'll go away from here.

1065
02:18:09.914 --> 02:18:14.977
Really? Okay, then...
Let's embrace.

1066
02:18:19.524 --> 02:18:22.493
Hurry up, Junga... I hold
the Queen of clubs.

1067
02:18:22.894 --> 02:18:28.264
That's okay, Samba. But look there;
the easy prey.

1068
02:19:01.132 --> 02:19:03.600
- Chief...
-Yes?

1069
02:19:04.035 --> 02:19:06.595
This boy's from Ramgarh.

1070
02:19:06.671 --> 02:19:10.471
He was on his way to the station,
when we found him.

1071
02:19:22.987 --> 02:19:30.758
Hear that, guys? People from Ramgarh
have started fleeiyg their homes!

1072
02:19:33.631 --> 02:19:38.432
Please... let me go.
I must...

1073
02:19:41.239 --> 02:19:43.139
Do you know me?

1074
02:19:43.975 --> 02:19:45.602
Do you?

1075
02:19:45.977 --> 02:19:50.038
I happey to be the
father of Ramgarh!

1076
02:19:53.084 --> 02:19:59.250
Well, Samba... these bastards have
their noses up in the air, don't they?

1077
02:20:00.091 --> 02:20:01.922
High up, indeed.

1078
02:20:02.894 --> 02:20:10.323
But I swear, I'll have them rub
their noses on the ground and...

1079
02:20:12.470 --> 02:20:17.498
You're going to grovel before me and
rub your nose on the ground now.

1080
02:20:18.777 --> 02:20:20.472
Come here.

1081
02:20:25.750 --> 02:20:27.183
Come here!

1082
02:20:27.619 --> 02:20:31.715
Hold in...!
He will bow on his own!

1083
02:20:36.694 --> 02:20:41.563
just watch what a dumb
son-of-a-bitch he is!

1084
02:20:42.400 --> 02:20:45.426
okay your knees, bloody swine!

1085
02:20:46.604 --> 02:20:48.128
Hold it!

1086
02:20:49.774 --> 02:20:53.642
Killiyg him with a bullen
would make things easy for him.

1087
02:20:54.679 --> 02:21:02.814
I'm going to torture
this bastard to death!

1088
02:22:34.913 --> 02:22:39.543
Why's there so much
of silence here?

1089
02:22:48.359 --> 02:22:50.793
- Imam-saheb...
- Who's that?

1090
02:22:52.363 --> 02:22:57.494
Veeru? Why's there so much
of silence here, son?

1091
02:22:59.103 --> 02:23:01.594
Please come with me.

1092
02:23:02.707 --> 02:23:05.073
- Please come...
- What's wrong?

1093
02:23:06.477 --> 02:23:10.675
What's up, son?
Where are you leading me...

1094
02:23:11.583 --> 02:23:12.914
Who's that?

1095
02:23:19.991 --> 02:23:21.549
Ahmed ?!

1096
02:23:24.896 --> 02:23:26.523
Ahmed!

1097
02:23:49.821 --> 02:23:53.279
lLmamsaheb, I must...

1098
02:23:53.358 --> 02:23:57.818
How will you console him, Thakur?
You're responsible for all this.

1099
02:23:58.329 --> 02:24:00.194
It's true!

1100
02:24:00.698 --> 02:24:06.034
nd you villagers had better listen
to this letter from Gabbar, too!

1101
02:24:06.337 --> 02:24:11.104
Addressed to the people of Ramgarh,
it says, "Look at the...''

1102
02:24:11.843 --> 02:24:15.904
"consequences of challenging me
at the Thakur's instigation''

1103
02:24:16.514 --> 02:24:20.143
"Should you folks still
not mend your ways...''

1104
02:24:20.518 --> 02:24:24.215
"death shall perform its ugly dance
in every courtyard of Ramgarh!''

1105
02:24:24.656 --> 02:24:29.116
"Should you care for the lives
of your family and children..''

1106
02:24:29.527 --> 02:24:31.791
"...then before sunrise tomorrow...''

1107
02:24:32.163 --> 02:24:37.601
"hand over the Thakur's men
to me, at the old hillock''

1108
02:24:37.935 --> 02:24:41.393
He has signed it off as "Gabbar
Singh, chief of the bandits.''

1109
02:24:41.873 --> 02:24:46.071
How could you land us in such
a grave danger, Thakur!

1110
02:24:56.454 --> 02:25:02.950
To lead an honorable life, we will
have to pay a price, Dinanath.

1111
02:25:04.062 --> 02:25:06.860
We are farmers, Thakur.

1112
02:25:07.598 --> 02:25:09.759
And we can pay the bandits
with food-grains for our lives.

1113
02:25:10.101 --> 02:25:11.796
We can't pay them with
our children's lives!

1114
02:25:12.170 --> 02:25:15.071
We're farmers, after all.
We are not soldiers.

1115
02:25:15.473 --> 02:25:19.273
You are right, Shankar.
We are indeed farmers.

1116
02:25:19.744 --> 02:25:23.305
This has been a country
of farmers for many ages.

1117
02:25:23.681 --> 02:25:27.412
But whenever someone evil has
shown aggressive designs...

1118
02:25:27.752 --> 02:25:32.553
...by God, it was farmers who
melted their ploughs into swords!

1119
02:25:34.525 --> 02:25:39.861
It's not the blood of cowards
that flows in our veins! No!

1120
02:25:39.931 --> 02:25:43.594
But how is violence and bloodshed
going to help?

1121
02:25:43.868 --> 02:25:46.132
Non-violence has its place, too.

1122
02:25:47.138 --> 02:25:49.231
I do believe in non-violence.

1123
02:25:49.474 --> 02:25:52.705
But it won't be an
act of non-violence...

1124
02:25:52.877 --> 02:25:54.310
...to grovel before
a wicked and evil man!

1125
02:25:54.545 --> 02:25:56.570
It's nothing but cowardliness!
Plain spinelessness!

1126
02:25:56.814 --> 02:26:00.011
Those who don't bow
are broken down, Thakur!

1127
02:26:00.284 --> 02:26:04.015
This Thakur can neither be made
to bow nor be broken down!

1128
02:26:05.089 --> 02:26:07.956
This Thakur can only die!

1129
02:26:09.260 --> 02:26:13.856
But I will live in dignity,
till as long as I live!

1130
02:26:14.098 --> 02:26:17.192
For how long are you going to live?
And how long will we live either...

1131
02:26:17.502 --> 02:26:20.266
...with these guys
around in the village?

1132
02:26:23.040 --> 02:26:28.945
If you think you can save
your children's lives...

1133
02:26:29.514 --> 02:26:30.947
...by handing us over
to Gabbar Singh...

1134
02:26:31.249 --> 02:26:34.980
...you can very well give us
up to Gabbar. We are willing.

1135
02:26:35.887 --> 02:26:38.617
Yes. We must do
the right thing now.

1136
02:26:38.923 --> 02:26:41.483
We can't bear the burden
of this problem anymore.

1137
02:26:45.129 --> 02:26:48.223
Who's speaking of not
bearing the burden?

1138
02:26:49.634 --> 02:26:53.695
Do you know what is the biggest
burden in the world?

1139
02:26:54.672 --> 02:26:58.472
A father bearing
the bier of his son!

1140
02:26:59.277 --> 02:27:01.302
There can be no bigger burden.

1141
02:27:01.913 --> 02:27:05.110
An old man like me is willing
to bear this burden...

1142
02:27:05.449 --> 02:27:11.217
...and you refuse
to combat a problem?

1143
02:27:12.256 --> 02:27:16.886
There's something I very
strongly believe in.

1144
02:27:17.595 --> 02:27:22.794
An honorable death is any day better
than a life of humiliation.

1145
02:27:24.435 --> 02:27:27.268
It's I, who has lost a son.

1146
02:27:27.972 --> 02:27:32.068
But I'd still want both of them
to stay on in this village.

1147
02:27:33.211 --> 02:27:36.578
I leave the rest to you.

1148
02:27:42.854 --> 02:27:45.584
It's time for my prayers.

1149
02:27:46.457 --> 02:27:49.483
I will ask God today
why He did not give me...

1150
02:27:49.694 --> 02:27:54.358
...some more sons to be
sacrificed for the village.

1151
02:27:57.068 --> 02:28:01.698
Will someone please help me
reach the mosque...?

1152
02:29:33.731 --> 02:29:35.926
What's that? A letter?

1153
02:29:36.000 --> 02:29:39.595
Of course, you idiot!
Read it.

1154
02:29:39.670 --> 02:29:45.768
"If you kill one villager, Gabbar,
we will slay four of your men''

1155
02:29:45.943 --> 02:29:51.040
Check out if it's those guys, or
have they dumped someone else here?

1156
02:30:27.485 --> 02:30:34.357
"For every villager you kill, Gabbar,
we will slay four of your men''

1157
02:30:46.637 --> 02:30:49.333
The fun begins now!

1158
02:30:50.307 --> 02:30:55.472
It's ages since I've run into
someone who boasts so much!

1159
02:30:56.580 --> 02:30:59.606
The real fun begins now!

1160
02:31:00.885 --> 02:31:07.620
This game will end with the
lives of these two guys.

1161
02:31:07.892 --> 02:31:11.328
Every family and household in
Ramgarh, will end with this, too!

1162
02:32:00.978 --> 02:32:02.172
Here you are.

1163
02:32:05.282 --> 02:32:07.375
It was really bothering you.

1164
02:32:24.268 --> 02:32:26.429
She's a very unfortunate girl.

1165
02:32:26.737 --> 02:32:30.468
It's almost as if she has
forgotten to speak.

1166
02:32:30.875 --> 02:32:33.173
As for earlier, I'm always reminded
of those days...

1167
02:32:33.577 --> 02:32:39.243
...when I first visited her village
with my master.

1168
02:32:40.751 --> 02:32:43.049
It was on the festival
of colors.

1169
02:32:43.420 --> 02:32:44.887
Hey! That's enough!

1170
02:32:45.623 --> 02:32:48.421
It's the festival of colors!
No one can take offense!

1171
02:32:49.927 --> 02:32:53.328
How will I celebrate with your father
if you douse all the colors on me?

1172
02:32:53.664 --> 02:32:56.132
How will you celebrane nhe fesnival
winh my fanher iy ayy case?

1173
02:32:56.433 --> 02:32:58.458
He just doesn't know how
to celebrate the festival!

1174
02:32:58.702 --> 02:33:01.227
He's been sitting at home
all day!

1175
02:33:01.472 --> 02:33:05.101
Either he touches the feet
of the elders visiting him...

1176
02:33:05.409 --> 02:33:07.934
...or the younger ones touch his
feet as a mark of respect.

1177
02:33:08.212 --> 02:33:12.273
They apply a pinch of color on each
other's forehead from a plate...

1178
02:33:12.550 --> 02:33:15.075
...embrace each other and
that's it! They've celebrated it!

1179
02:33:15.319 --> 02:33:19.346
That's no way of doing it!
It's us, who really celebrate it!

1180
02:33:19.690 --> 02:33:21.715
Really? And how do
you celebrate it?

1181
02:33:21.992 --> 02:33:25.393
You know Paro, don't you?

1182
02:33:25.496 --> 02:33:27.589
- Paro?
-Yes! Paro!

1183
02:33:27.865 --> 02:33:33.303
There's a tank in her courtyard.
We've mixed all the colors in it!

1184
02:33:33.537 --> 02:33:35.368
Where folks normally douse
color on people...

1185
02:33:35.606 --> 02:33:38.632
...we dump people
in the colours!

1186
02:33:38.842 --> 02:33:42.903
The moment we spot someone,
he goes straight in the tank!

1187
02:33:43.581 --> 02:33:46.880
I hope you don't have a tank
of colors in your house!

1188
02:33:47.418 --> 02:33:49.682
Or Ramlal and I will find
ourselves neck-deep in it.

1189
02:33:52.623 --> 02:33:54.523
Watch what I do!

1190
02:33:54.625 --> 02:33:56.388
Anyone in, mister?

1191
02:33:57.061 --> 02:33:58.187
Who's that?

1192
02:34:00.464 --> 02:34:02.455
- I've scared you again!
- You're crazy!

1193
02:34:03.067 --> 02:34:05.763
The Thakur!
You didn't even tell me!

1194
02:34:06.036 --> 02:34:08.971
Welcome! Greenings of the season!

1195
02:34:10.374 --> 02:34:12.899
What are you standing there for?

1196
02:34:13.143 --> 02:34:15.873
Won't you bring some sweets
for the Thakur?

1197
02:34:16.113 --> 02:34:17.273
Just a moment...

1198
02:34:17.848 --> 02:34:19.475
- Must I bring the plate too?
- Which one?

1199
02:34:19.717 --> 02:34:22.686
The one from which you will
take a pinch of color...

1200
02:34:22.987 --> 02:34:24.386
Sure, go ahead and bring it.

1201
02:34:25.789 --> 02:34:27.552
Please come, Thakur.

1202
02:34:27.825 --> 02:34:32.353
Let's go and sit there...
it's very loud out here.

1203
02:34:33.797 --> 02:34:37.164
- So, Ramlal? Is everything fine?
- I'm fine, thank you, sir.

1204
02:34:38.202 --> 02:34:40.796
Well, Thakur? I hope you've
had a nice crop this year

1205
02:34:41.071 --> 02:34:43.539
Actually, I'm an outsider
in my own house.

1206
02:34:43.807 --> 02:34:47.334
It's Ramlal who knows everything
about my farms.

1207
02:34:47.611 --> 02:34:50.580
It's he who commands things
in our farms.

1208
02:34:51.382 --> 02:34:55.512
Sweets for everyone!

1209
02:34:55.786 --> 02:34:57.583
Open your mouth, uncle!

1210
02:34:59.089 --> 02:35:00.556
That's enough, dear...

1211
02:35:01.025 --> 02:35:03.687
Okay, Mr. Ramlal...
open your mouth!

1212
02:35:04.128 --> 02:35:05.789
- Give it to me, dear. I'll have it.
- No, sir!

1213
02:35:05.896 --> 02:35:08.694
- I will feed you!
- Give it to me, dear.

1214
02:35:09.099 --> 02:35:12.432
She's like your daughter, Ramlal.
Let her feed you.

1215
02:35:12.536 --> 02:35:15.869
He's right. Now open your mouth!

1216
02:35:18.409 --> 02:35:21.401
My God! How could I forget the
plate with the colors?

1217
02:35:22.680 --> 02:35:24.204
She's a very jovial girl.

1218
02:35:24.448 --> 02:35:28.214
You bet! She's always
kicking up a racket!

1219
02:35:28.519 --> 02:35:31.920
Here I come with
the plate of colors!

1220
02:35:32.523 --> 02:35:35.981
Here's the plate of colors for you
to take a pinch out of it!

1221
02:35:36.427 --> 02:35:39.760
- I'm leaving!
- Where are you going?

1222
02:35:40.731 --> 02:35:44.462
I'm going to my friends to celebrate!
May I leave?

1223
02:35:45.836 --> 02:35:48.361
Haven't you had enough
of the colors yet?

1224
02:35:49.873 --> 02:35:55.505
It's a festival of colors, uncle...
of all hues!

1225
02:35:55.746 --> 02:35:57.976
How can anyone ever have
enough of the colors?

1226
02:35:58.248 --> 02:36:00.079
Tell me; wouldn't the world be
so dull, without these colors?

1227
02:36:00.150 --> 02:36:03.278
How dull and lifeless her world
has suddenly come to be.

1228
02:36:09.393 --> 02:36:13.693
With her tears having washed away
her bridal-henna...

1229
02:36:14.465 --> 02:36:21.200
...what colors can
she look forward to in life?

1230
02:37:48.759 --> 02:37:55.494
I've taken a decision.

1231
02:37:56.200 --> 02:37:59.692
Really? So you've started
taking decisions too?!

1232
02:38:00.404 --> 02:38:04.465
Yes. When you are into it,
I think I'd rather do it too.

1233
02:38:05.008 --> 02:38:07.374
- What is that?
- Get married.

1234
02:38:09.012 --> 02:38:10.673
Get married?!

1235
02:38:12.149 --> 02:38:13.616
You want to get married?!

1236
02:38:14.451 --> 02:38:16.681
Yes... I've had enough.

1237
02:38:17.221 --> 02:38:20.918
I've now decided to lead
a straight and simple life.

1238
02:38:21.225 --> 02:38:25.355
In which I have a house of my own,
a wife, many children...

1239
02:38:25.729 --> 02:38:27.720
...who will pester you
for stories...

1240
02:38:27.831 --> 02:38:32.734
Hey! That's enough!
Sit down here, will you?

1241
02:38:32.803 --> 02:38:35.499
Sit down here, I say.

1242
02:38:36.173 --> 02:38:41.770
I hope you know that you need
a girl to get married to?

1243
02:38:42.179 --> 02:38:44.545
Have you approved of a girl then?

1244
02:38:45.549 --> 02:38:48.780
- Yes, I have.
- Who is she, may I ask?

1245
02:38:51.054 --> 02:38:54.421
Than Radha?!

1246
02:38:55.826 --> 02:38:58.317
Are you mad? Don't you know
who she is?

1247
02:38:59.296 --> 02:39:05.565
Now look; even thugs and criminals
are given a second chance in life.

1248
02:39:06.270 --> 02:39:08.363
And then, Radha has done
nothing wrong.

1249
02:39:08.705 --> 02:39:11.367
Has she no right to start
life afresh?

1250
02:39:11.475 --> 02:39:16.572
How can that be? What will society
and community think of it?

1251
02:39:16.980 --> 02:39:23.010
The society and community are meant
to save man from loneliness.

1252
02:39:23.954 --> 02:39:26.388
They're not meant to
isolate someone.

1253
02:39:27.190 --> 02:39:32.651
Besides, must we let Radha suffer
in silence for fear of society?

1254
02:39:34.531 --> 02:39:38.934
How long are we going to live
anyway? We might soon be dead.

1255
02:39:39.970 --> 02:39:44.430
Whose support will she live on?
Whom will she turn to?

1256
02:39:45.709 --> 02:39:48.644
It was because of all this
that I came to you.

1257
02:39:48.946 --> 02:39:53.508
But you are her father.
I leave the decision to you.

1258
02:39:53.584 --> 02:39:56.678
Not at all, Thakur.
She's your daughter now.

1259
02:39:57.588 --> 02:40:01.547
Whatever you decide will be
best for her.

1260
02:40:02.426 --> 02:40:06.385
I'll send him over
in a couple of days.

1261
02:40:07.197 --> 02:40:09.995
I'll send him over
in a couple of days.

1262
02:40:25.582 --> 02:40:27.914
A penny for your thoughts!

1263
02:40:30.454 --> 02:40:32.115
It's nothing.

1264
02:40:32.322 --> 02:40:36.759
I get it! I know what
you're worrying about.

1265
02:40:37.527 --> 02:40:41.486
You're wondering whether your
proposal will come through.

1266
02:40:42.432 --> 02:40:44.559
I suggest you toss again.

1267
02:40:45.502 --> 02:40:48.198
If it's Heads, it's gonna
be okay. Or else... well!

1268
02:40:51.575 --> 02:40:57.070
If everything works out
well, Veeru...

1269
02:40:58.982 --> 02:41:01.473
...why don't we settle down here,
in this village?

1270
02:41:01.652 --> 02:41:04.485
There! You've spoken my heart!

1271
02:41:04.755 --> 02:41:07.019
I've been thinking of this, too.

1272
02:41:07.491 --> 02:41:09.755
It's no use being thieves
all our lives.

1273
02:41:10.093 --> 02:41:12.084
We've spent enough time
in the prisons.

1274
02:41:12.362 --> 02:41:14.387
Once we get the money,
let's settle down here.

1275
02:41:14.498 --> 02:41:18.298
We'll buy some land and
turn farmers.

1276
02:41:19.436 --> 02:41:23.964
But we can't use the plough...
how will we be farmers?

1277
02:41:25.876 --> 02:41:30.404
Our vices taught us to wield guns;
our virtues will teach us this.

1278
02:41:30.480 --> 02:41:34.177
You're right. Necessity does
teach a man a lot in life.

1279
02:41:34.418 --> 02:41:36.716
I've already worked out
everything for myself!

1280
02:41:36.987 --> 02:41:38.716
I'll marry the girl
who drives the horse-cart...

1281
02:41:38.922 --> 02:41:42.085
...and be the father of a
couple of children in 2/3 years.

1282
02:41:42.392 --> 02:41:44.690
I've even thought
of the brats' names!

1283
02:41:44.961 --> 02:41:49.022
And when I ask my wife
where the kids are...

1284
02:41:49.299 --> 02:41:50.698
She'll say...

1285
02:41:50.767 --> 02:41:55.204
"They must be with your friend Jai
to listen to his stories''

1286
02:41:57.007 --> 02:42:01.808
Why must you always send your
children to me for stories?

1287
02:42:01.945 --> 02:42:06.382
You know I can't remember
these bloody stories, Jai!

1288
02:42:06.650 --> 02:42:10.746
Stories, my foot! You don't even
remember what happened yesterday.

1289
02:42:11.254 --> 02:42:14.883
Yesterday? Of course I remember
I met Basanti yesterday!

1290
02:42:15.158 --> 02:42:18.457
We've promised to meet
at the lake this morning!

1291
02:42:19.096 --> 02:42:21.121
- This morning, huh?
- Yes!

1292
02:42:22.432 --> 02:42:23.831
Here I go!

1293
02:42:42.819 --> 02:42:44.844
Let's go, Dhanno!

1294
02:42:54.064 --> 02:42:58.899
Let's go! It's a question
of my chastity today!

1295
02:43:25.428 --> 02:43:29.330
Go on, Dhanno! Faster!

1296
02:44:06.570 --> 02:44:09.630
Faster, Dhanno! Go for it!

1297
02:48:05.775 --> 02:48:11.611
What do these guys in Ramgarh
feed their daughters with?

1298
02:48:12.415 --> 02:48:15.578
Look at her... she's one hell
of a spicy doll, isn't she?

1299
02:48:16.119 --> 02:48:21.113
Damn spicy, all right!

1300
02:48:21.858 --> 02:48:26.921
Remember how we went to Jamnadas's
daughter's wedding last year, chief?

1301
02:48:27.030 --> 02:48:28.964
She'd given them a terrific
dance performance there.

1302
02:48:29.032 --> 02:48:30.465
Wow!

1303
02:48:32.635 --> 02:48:35.502
She must be a sizzling dancer!

1304
02:48:35.872 --> 02:48:39.899
Show us a couple
of steps, darling.

1305
02:48:40.810 --> 02:48:44.769
Now look, lady... don't you
act too high and mighty!

1306
02:48:45.148 --> 02:48:50.415
Or I'll scratch off this
beautiful skin... all right?

1307
02:48:58.795 --> 02:49:00.695
Wait a minute, darling.

1308
02:49:04.667 --> 02:49:07.067
Tie the bastard!

1309
02:49:15.044 --> 02:49:18.343
You seem to be thick with him,
what say?

1310
02:49:25.421 --> 02:49:31.360
Well, strong man? Mohammad
comes to the mountain, eh?

1311
02:49:37.000 --> 02:49:39.560
You have a scene with
that babe, do you?

1312
02:49:39.802 --> 02:49:45.798
You bastard! I've yet to see
a creep like you!

1313
02:49:46.276 --> 02:49:48.972
You won't get to see one either.

1314
02:49:51.314 --> 02:49:54.647
Because your life is
now going to end.

1315
02:49:54.918 --> 02:49:57.284
- The bastard...
- No!

1316
02:50:08.965 --> 02:50:12.526
Like a house on fire, eh?

1317
02:50:17.173 --> 02:50:20.108
You're pretty thick, aren't you?

1318
02:50:21.578 --> 02:50:25.742
Pick up your gun, Samba!

1319
02:50:28.985 --> 02:50:32.352
And aim your gun at this cur!

1320
02:50:35.425 --> 02:50:37.290
Now listen to me, darling.

1321
02:50:37.560 --> 02:50:43.931
If you wish to save your lover,
show us some dance.

1322
02:50:44.100 --> 02:50:48.628
No! Don't you dare dance
before this dogs, Basanti!

1323
02:50:55.144 --> 02:50:59.945
Delay this any longer, and we'll
blow your lover's head apart!

1324
02:51:00.717 --> 02:51:04.778
There's another thing
I must tell you, darling.

1325
02:51:05.188 --> 02:51:09.682
That man will breathe,
only till you continue to dance.

1326
02:51:10.693 --> 02:51:15.653
That gun will go off, the
moment your feet stop moving.

1327
02:57:17.860 --> 02:57:21.489
If anyone dare moves,
he's gonna be dead meat!

1328
02:57:24.033 --> 02:57:29.198
abbar Singh! Ask your men
to drop their guns!

1329
02:57:32.708 --> 02:57:34.300
Go on

1330
02:58:56.158 --> 02:58:58.888
Go after them! Go on!

1331
02:58:59.195 --> 02:59:02.096
And don't return empty-handed,
you bastards!

1332
02:59:03.466 --> 02:59:05.661
Hurry up!

1333
03:00:37.126 --> 03:00:39.788
-jai! Are you all right?
-Yes, I'm okay.

1334
03:00:44.099 --> 03:00:46.795
The three of us can't escape
on a single horse, Veeru.

1335
03:00:47.136 --> 03:00:51.004
Take Basanti away to the village
and return soon.

1336
03:00:51.640 --> 03:00:54.507
And bring lots of ammunition
when you return.

1337
03:00:57.246 --> 03:01:01.046
No! I will stay here!
Take Basanti and leave quickly!

1338
03:01:01.851 --> 03:01:05.116
Listen to me, Veeru!
Take Basanti away! I'll stay here.

1339
03:01:06.155 --> 03:01:08.646
No, Jai! I can't leave you alone.

1340
03:01:08.958 --> 03:01:11.051
ryye of us will have no go, Veeru.

1341
03:01:11.360 --> 03:01:13.590
Or else, we'll soon
run out of bullets.

1342
03:01:15.064 --> 03:01:17.965
Well, all right.
Let's toss instead.

1343
03:01:18.033 --> 03:01:22.060
If it's Heads, I stay back.
If it's Tails, you hold fort.

1344
03:01:25.608 --> 03:01:27.200
I win!

1345
03:01:31.313 --> 03:01:33.474
- But how can you be...
- No more arguments, Veeru!

1346
03:01:33.682 --> 03:01:37.243
Leave your gun and bullets behind.
And take Basanti out quickly! Go on!

1347
03:01:43.759 --> 03:01:46.694
I somehow don't feel like
leaving you alone, Jai.

1348
03:01:46.896 --> 03:01:49.990
- Take care, okay?
- Sure.

1349
03:05:47.336 --> 03:05:48.667
There's just one bullet!

1350
03:06:58.073 --> 03:07:01.600
- Are you okay, Jai?!
- Yes... I'm okay.

1351
03:07:05.647 --> 03:07:08.047
I've killed every
single bastard before...

1352
03:07:09.351 --> 03:07:13.515
Don't worry, Jai!
Just don't be scared!

1353
03:07:13.922 --> 03:07:17.414
Why must I be scared when
you're with me, Veeru?

1354
03:07:18.093 --> 03:07:21.028
Let's return to our village!
Everything will be all right!

1355
03:07:21.530 --> 03:07:24.966
My game is up, Veeru.

1356
03:07:25.200 --> 03:07:26.690
-- It's all over...
- No!

1357
03:07:27.703 --> 03:07:30.797
No, Jai! Don't say such things!

1358
03:07:31.773 --> 03:07:35.368
But I have no regrets, Veeru.

1359
03:07:35.644 --> 03:07:39.671
I have lived for my friend...
and am dying before him!

1360
03:07:40.249 --> 03:07:44.185
But there is something
I'm leaving unfinished, Veeru.

1361
03:07:44.553 --> 03:07:46.384
I won't be able to tell
stories to your children.

1362
03:07:46.488 --> 03:07:49.924
You're going to be all right, Jai!
Nothing will happen to you!

1363
03:07:50.892 --> 03:07:55.056
But you must tell your children
tales of our friendship and exploits.

1364
03:07:55.464 --> 03:07:57.489
You won't forget that, will you?

1365
03:07:57.599 --> 03:07:59.624
Whan yoyseyse are you nalkiyg?!

1366
03:08:04.273 --> 03:08:06.901
Look there, Veeru...

1367
03:08:13.148 --> 03:08:15.981
There's yet another
incomplete story, Veeru.

1368
03:08:16.652 --> 03:08:19.678
What had I dreamed of;
and what has come to be?

1369
03:08:19.788 --> 03:08:26.057
No, Jai!
You can't leave me like this!

1370
03:08:26.161 --> 03:08:27.492
No!

1371
03:08:32.301 --> 03:08:34.166
No, Jai! Please don't!

1372
03:08:34.236 --> 03:08:36.636
No, Jai!
You can't do this to me!

1373
03:11:21.703 --> 03:11:28.472
Jai! You have cheated me
to save my life?

1374
03:11:34.149 --> 03:11:37.312
I swear upon the blood
that you have shed!

1375
03:11:38.019 --> 03:11:42.854
I will pick and choose each
one of them, and give them death!

1376
03:11:43.825 --> 03:11:47.192
Gabbar Singh!
I'm coming after you!

1377
03:12:26.368 --> 03:12:29.997
Run! But how far
will you go, you swine!

1378
03:13:24.893 --> 03:13:27.828
Gabbar! Come out in the open!

1379
03:13:28.763 --> 03:13:31.755
Face me like a man,
you bastard!

1380
03:13:32.133 --> 03:13:37.161
I've come to avenge every drop
of blood that my friend has shed!

1381
03:13:37.272 --> 03:13:40.605
You can't escape death today!

1382
03:15:31.953 --> 03:15:34.478
Hand him over to me, Veeru.

1383
03:15:34.889 --> 03:15:40.350
No, Thakur! I'm not going to
let this bastard live anymore!

1384
03:15:40.528 --> 03:15:42.155
Doy'n forgen your promise, Veeru!

1385
03:15:42.397 --> 03:15:44.365
I don't remember anything!

1386
03:15:44.599 --> 03:15:49.195
All I know is that this bastard's
men have killed my friend!

1387
03:15:49.404 --> 03:15:52.202
And I'm going to have
his blood for that!

1388
03:15:52.407 --> 03:15:56.207
It was that very friend of yours
who had made a promise to me.

1389
03:15:58.480 --> 03:16:01.074
Leave him alone.

1390
03:16:12.494 --> 03:16:18.057
I wish it was I who had made the
promise; I'd have broken it today!

1391
03:16:18.399 --> 03:16:21.994
But it was my friend
who gave you his word.

1392
03:16:22.070 --> 03:16:23.560
So,...

1393
03:17:09.818 --> 03:17:16.747
You can't fight me, Thakur!
I've already cut your arms!

1394
03:17:17.992 --> 03:17:23.589
One uses his feet, not his hands,
to crush the snake, Gabbar!

1395
03:17:25.066 --> 03:17:29.059
My feen are eyough
no deal winh you!

1396
03:17:50.558 --> 03:17:54.085
Your arms are full of
strength, aren't they?

1397
03:19:06.134 --> 03:19:10.264
Gabbar! Give your hands to me!

1398
03:19:10.471 --> 03:19:11.802
No!

1399
03:19:13.441 --> 03:19:15.636
Give me this hand, Gabbarr!

1400
03:19:15.777 --> 03:19:17.836
No!

1401
03:23:41.042 --> 03:23:45.308
Well, Thakur...
I must leave now.

1402
03:23:49.717 --> 03:23:55.087
I know I can't share your grief;
But I do
